1
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:51,585
[ Girl ]
HAND ME THE FLASHLIGHT.
[ Girl

2
00:00:51,619 --> 00:00:53,487
[ Girls Giggling ]

3
00:00:53,521 --> 00:00:57,558
KIT,
I'VE GOT THE SHOVEL.
YOU DO ?

4
00:00:57,591 --> 00:01:00,694
LUCY,
GET THE BOX.
OKAY.

5
00:01:00,728 --> 00:01:05,333
WHAT ARE YOU PUTTIN' IN ?
IT'S SUPPOSED
TO BE A SECRET.

6
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:11,805
MY DAD THINKS
I'M AT YOUR HOUSE.
MY MOM THINKS I'M AT YOURS.

7
00:01:11,839 --> 00:01:15,709
[ Lucy ]
LET'S DIG DEEP.
OKAY.

8
00:01:15,743 --> 00:01:19,680
SO NO ONE WILL FIND IT.

9
00:01:21,149 --> 00:01:25,719
DIG IT DEEPER !
SHH.
WE DON'T WANNA GET CAUGHT.

10
00:01:25,753 --> 00:01:28,289
I WANT SOME DIRT.

11
00:01:30,758 --> 00:01:34,562
[ Young Woman Narrating ]
WHEN WE WERE TEN GROWING UP
IN GEORGIA,

12
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:39,900
MIMI, KIT AND I KNEW EXACTLY
WHAT WE WANTED OUT OF LIFE.

13
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:42,603
LUCY, GET THE BOX.
[ Mimi ]
THIS IS FUN.

14
00:01:42,636 --> 00:01:47,875
[ Lucy Narrating ]
SO WE PUT OUR DREAMS IN A BOX,
AND WE BURIED IT.

15
00:01:47,908 --> 00:01:52,180
WE HAVE TO KEEP IT DRY.

16
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,923
[ Lucy Narrating ]
WE MADE A PACT TO DIG IT UP
AT MIDNIGHT...

17
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:06,427
THE DAY OF OUR
HIGH SCHOOL GRADUATION.

18
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,796
PACK IT DOWN.

19
00:02:10,931 --> 00:02:14,735
LET'S BE BEST FRIENDS
FOREVER.
WE WILL.

20
00:02:14,768 --> 00:02:18,339
[ Lucy Narrating ]
NOW, I DON'T EVEN REMEMBER
WHAT OUR WISHES WERE--

21
00:02:18,372 --> 00:02:20,274
EXCEPT FOR ONE.

22
00:02:20,308 --> 00:02:24,245
WE WISHED THAT WE'D BE
BEST FRIENDS FOREVER.

23
00:02:24,278 --> 00:02:28,416
WELL, THAT WISH
DIDN'T COME TRUE.

24
00:02:46,267 --> 00:02:53,274
** [ Singing With Radio ]
* I SEE YOU ON THE STREET
AND YOU WALK ON BY *

25
00:02:53,307 --> 00:02:54,942
* BABY

26
00:02:54,975 --> 00:03:00,214
* YOU MAKE ME WANNA HANG
MY HEAD DOWN AND CRY *

27
00:03:03,651 --> 00:03:07,688
* IF YOU GAVE ME
HALF A CHANCE, YOU'D SEE *

28
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:11,892
* MY DESIRE BURNING
INSIDE OF ME *

29
00:03:11,925 --> 00:03:16,930
* BUT YOU CHOOSE
TO LOOK THE OTHER WAY *

30
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:23,404
* I'VE HAD TO WORK
MUCH HARDER THAN THIS *

31
00:03:23,437 --> 00:03:27,708
* FOR SOMETHING I WANT
DON'T TRY TO RESIST ME *

32
00:03:27,741 --> 00:03:31,545
* OPEN YOUR HEART TO ME, BABY

33
00:03:31,579 --> 00:03:35,816
* I HOLD THE LOCK
AND YOU HOLD THE KEY-- **

34
00:03:35,849 --> 00:03:38,286
[ Man ]
LUCILLE WAGNER !
POP ?

35
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:41,322
- BABY, WE'RE GONNA BE LATE.
- I WAS JUST--

36
00:03:41,355 --> 00:03:43,357
- DID YOU PRACTICE YOUR SPEECH ?
- I ALMOST HAVE IT.

37
00:03:43,391 --> 00:03:46,427
LUCY, HOW'S IT GONNA LOOK
IF THE VALEDICTORIAN
MESSES UP HER SPEECH ?

38
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,961
OKAY.

39
00:03:47,995 --> 00:03:51,399
DON'T WRINKLE YOUR ROBE.
JUST IRONED IT FOR YA.

40
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:58,472
OKAY, BIG DAY ! COME ON !
SEE YA ON DECK ! LET'S GO !

41
00:03:58,506 --> 00:04:01,542
TOADS DO LOOK LIKE FROGS.

42
00:04:01,575 --> 00:04:04,478
IT'S JUST ONE'S, YOU KNOW,
IN THE WATER AND ONE'S NOT.

43
00:04:04,512 --> 00:04:07,047
IT DOESN'T--
IT COULD HAPPEN TO ANYBODY.

44
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,984
HEY, MIMI !
I KNOW YOU WANT ME.

45
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:15,889
HO !

46
00:04:15,923 --> 00:04:18,025
I'M GONNA LOOK
DROP-DEAD GORGEOUS.

47
00:04:18,058 --> 00:04:21,028
YOU SHOULD SEE MY DRESS.

48
00:04:21,061 --> 00:04:25,299
- HELLO ! CAN YOU JUST WATCH
WHERE YOU'RE GOING ?
- YOU RAN INTO ME, KIT.

49
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:27,668
WHAT, YOU'RE TOO PERFECT
TO BUMP INTO ANYBODY ?

50
00:04:27,701 --> 00:04:29,803
WHAT ?
PERFECT.

51
00:04:29,837 --> 00:04:33,641
SWEET, PROPER,

52
00:04:33,674 --> 00:04:35,909
NERDY AND VIRGINAL.

53
00:04:35,943 --> 00:04:38,579
I'M NOT--
YOU'RE A VIRGIN.

54
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:41,349
I TOLD Y'ALL.

55
00:04:41,382 --> 00:04:44,918
JUST GET US
IN THE PICTURE, OKAY ?
NOW-- HOLD MY PURSE.

56
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:48,789
NO, DON'T PUSH THE BUTTON.
WAIT TILL I GET OVER THERE.
HONEY !

57
00:04:48,822 --> 00:04:54,362
MAMA, WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?
JUST ONE SECOND.
STAND UP STRAIGHT.

58
00:04:54,395 --> 00:04:57,798
I AM. I WILL.
TUCK YOUR TUMMY IN.

59
00:04:57,831 --> 00:04:59,933
- SMILE.
- MOM, I'M SMILING !

60
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:02,536
BIGGER, DARLING.

61
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:06,407
- LUCY, YOUR SPEECH
WAS WONDERFUL.
- THANK YOU.

62
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,976
I HOPE YOU'RE GONNA CONTINUE
STUDYING MUSIC IN COLLEGE.

63
00:05:09,009 --> 00:05:11,044
ACTUALLY, LUCY WANTS
TO BECOME A DOCTOR.

64
00:05:11,078 --> 00:05:13,947
VOICE CLASSES WOULD MAKE
NICE ELECTIVES.

65
00:05:13,981 --> 00:05:17,084
NOT MUCH TIME.
WE'RE LOOKING AT A DOUBLE MAJOR
IN BIOLOGY AND CHEMISTRY...

66
00:05:17,117 --> 00:05:21,722
IF SHE WANTS TO GET INTO
THE BEST MED SCHOOL, HUH ?

67
00:05:21,755 --> 00:05:24,825
HENRY, COME ON, I'LL SHOW
YOU HOW TO START THAT TRUCK
FOR TONIGHT.

68
00:05:24,858 --> 00:05:27,961
ALL RIGHT.
SEE YOU LATER.
OKAY.

69
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:31,399
BYE, MS. "J."
GOOD LUCK, HENRY.

70
00:05:32,866 --> 00:05:34,835
I'M ALL HE'S GOT,
YOU KNOW ?

71
00:05:34,868 --> 00:05:39,072
CONGRATULATIONS, LUCY.

72
00:05:39,106 --> 00:05:42,109
THANK YOU.
THANKS.

73
00:05:47,781 --> 00:05:49,850
[ Knock At Door ]

74
00:05:49,883 --> 00:05:55,556
HERE IT IS.
HONEY, WHAT'S WRONG ?

75
00:05:55,589 --> 00:05:57,124
I'M FINE.

76
00:05:58,726 --> 00:06:03,764
POP, I WORKED REALLY HARD
TO BE THE VALEDICTORIAN.

77
00:06:03,797 --> 00:06:06,033
COURSE YOU DID.

78
00:06:07,901 --> 00:06:09,970
WHY DIDN'T IT FEEL
LIKE ANYTHING ?

79
00:06:10,003 --> 00:06:13,907
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
YOU DIDN'T FEEL ANYTHING ?
IT FELT GREAT !

80
00:06:15,175 --> 00:06:18,178
POP, I NEVER WENT
TO ONE FOOTBALL GAME.

81
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:20,614
YOU DON'T LIKE FOOTBALL.

82
00:06:20,648 --> 00:06:24,485
BUT YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO GO,
AND IT'S SUPPOSED TO BE FUN.

83
00:06:24,518 --> 00:06:28,422
AND LIKE ALL THE PARTIES
AT HEMMINGS FIELD
AND STUFF,

84
00:06:28,456 --> 00:06:31,058
I NEVER WENT
TO ANY OF 'EM.

85
00:06:31,091 --> 00:06:36,196
I NEVER STAYED OUT LATE.
I NEVER JUST... HUNG OUT.

86
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:38,766
'CAUSE YOU HAD
A HEAD ON YOUR SHOULDERS.

87
00:06:38,799 --> 00:06:40,701
YOU STAYED HOME,
AND YOU STUDIED.

88
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:44,672
THERE'S JUST A LOT OF THINGS
THAT I WANTED TO DO
THAT I DIDN'T.

89
00:06:46,206 --> 00:06:49,810
AND I WAS UP THERE
GETTING MY DIPLOMA,
AND I WAS LIKE...

90
00:06:49,843 --> 00:06:51,779
"IS THIS IT ?"

91
00:06:51,812 --> 00:06:56,049
COME ON NOW.
DIDN'T WE BOTH WORK HARD
FOR THIS ?

92
00:06:56,083 --> 00:07:00,187
OH.
YOU'RE RIGHT.

93
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:04,525
I GUESS IT'S JUST
THE PRESSURE OF GRADUATION
AND ALL. YOU'RE RIGHT.

94
00:07:12,099 --> 00:07:15,002
GIRLS, HI !

95
00:07:18,839 --> 00:07:21,041
LUCY.

96
00:07:28,982 --> 00:07:31,118
MIMI, NOT NOW.
OKAY ?

97
00:07:31,151 --> 00:07:34,121
- ARE YOU COMIN' OR NOT ?
- COMING WHERE ?

98
00:07:34,154 --> 00:07:36,089
IT'S GRADUATION NIGHT !

99
00:07:36,123 --> 00:07:40,127
OH, GOD, HEMMINGS FIELD.
I TOTALLY FORGOT.

100
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,896
SO, ARE YOU COMIN'
OR NOT ?

101
00:07:42,930 --> 00:07:45,098
HI.
HEY.

102
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:48,869
I HAVE PLANS.
I'M SORRY.

103
00:07:48,902 --> 00:07:51,839
COME ON.
YOU OKAY ?

104
00:07:51,872 --> 00:07:53,841
I'M OKAY.

105
00:08:01,248 --> 00:08:03,717
DO YOU WANT SOMETHING ?

106
00:08:03,751 --> 00:08:06,720
YEAH. ARE YOU COMING
AT MIDNIGHT OR WHAT ?

107
00:08:07,888 --> 00:08:11,859
EXCUSE ME ?
KIT, WE MADE A PACT,
REMEMBER ?

108
00:08:11,892 --> 00:08:15,162
OH, YOU'RE NOT SERIOUS !

109
00:08:16,564 --> 00:08:19,600
WELL, LOOK, YOU CAN
REALLY GO WITHOUT ME.

110
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:23,637
I HAVE BETTER THINGS TO DO
THAN DIG UP SOME OLD BOX.

111
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:30,544
* STANDING HERE
LOOKING AT ALL THE WORLD *

112
00:08:30,578 --> 00:08:34,782
** [ Continues Indistinct ]

113
00:08:40,688 --> 00:08:44,191
THE GUITAR GUY
IS SUCH A HOTTIE.

114
00:08:44,224 --> 00:08:48,696
- THAT'S BEN KIMBLE.
- I HEARD HE JUST GOT OUT
OF JAIL. KILLED A GUY.

115
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:52,032
I DON'T BELIEVE YOU.

116
00:08:52,065 --> 00:08:55,202
YEAH ! EVERYBODY'S TALKING
ABOUT IT.

117
00:08:55,235 --> 00:08:57,170
OH, TOO BAD !

118
00:08:57,204 --> 00:09:00,040
WELL, IF ANYONE COULD HAVE HIM,
IT'D BE YOU.

119
00:09:00,073 --> 00:09:03,644
BUT I'M OFF THE MARKET,
REMEMBER ?

120
00:09:03,677 --> 00:09:06,747
OH, PLEASE !
DYLAN'S AT UCLA DOING...

121
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:10,651
GOD KNOWS WHAT
WITH GOD KNOWS WHO.
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

122
00:09:10,684 --> 00:09:11,985
RIGHT.

123
00:09:12,019 --> 00:09:14,087
WHATEVER.

124
00:09:15,956 --> 00:09:19,727
[ Lucy ]
ARE YOU READY ?
YEAH, YEAH, JUST TWO SECONDS.

125
00:09:25,132 --> 00:09:29,336
OKAY, HOLD ON.

126
00:09:29,369 --> 00:09:32,940
HENRY, ARE YOU READY ?

127
00:09:32,973 --> 00:09:35,743
* I'VE BEEN REALLY TRYIN'
BABY *

128
00:09:35,776 --> 00:09:37,845
I'M READY.

129
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:44,885
* TRYIN' TO HOLD BACK
THIS FEELIN' FOR SO LONG *

130
00:09:45,986 --> 00:09:48,255
[ Giggling ]

131
00:09:48,288 --> 00:09:51,224
* AND IF YOU FEEL
LIKE I FEEL, BABY *

132
00:09:51,258 --> 00:09:56,263
* COME ON
OH, COME ON *

133
00:09:56,296 --> 00:10:00,400
* LET'S GET IT ON
AH, BABY *

134
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,903
* LET'S GET IT ON

135
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:04,738
THAT'S OKAY.
GO ON.

136
00:10:04,772 --> 00:10:08,408
* LET'S LOVE, BABY
OKAY.

137
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:11,712
* LET'S GET IT ON

138
00:10:11,745 --> 00:10:15,916
* SUGAR, LET'S
GET IT ON-- **

139
00:10:17,885 --> 00:10:23,056
WHY ARE YOU STOPPING ?
HENRY, THIS ISN'T HOW
I HOPED IT WOULD BE.

140
00:10:23,090 --> 00:10:28,295
THAT'S WEIRD, 'CAUSE
THIS IS EXACTLY HOW I HOPED
IT WOULD BE, OR PRETTY ACCURATE.

141
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:30,998
MAYBE IF WE GET INTO BED.

142
00:10:31,031 --> 00:10:34,001
OOH ! THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.

143
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:38,005
OKAY.

144
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:40,808
THESE ARE NICE SHEETS.

145
00:10:42,776 --> 00:10:45,445
CAN I HEAR THE LIST AGAIN ?
OH, LUCE, COME ON.

146
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:49,182
PLEASE, PLEASE.
JUST ONE MORE TIME.

147
00:10:49,216 --> 00:10:52,720
OKAY.

148
00:10:52,753 --> 00:10:54,822
THANKS.

149
00:10:54,855 --> 00:10:57,024
** [ Music Off ]
ALL RIGHT.

150
00:10:59,126 --> 00:11:01,228
[ Clears Throat ]

151
00:11:01,261 --> 00:11:06,800
REASON NUMBER ONE: WE'VE BEEN
LAB PARTNERS FOR THREE YEARS
SO WE REALLY TRUST EACH OTHER.

152
00:11:06,834 --> 00:11:09,903
THAT'S REALLY IMPORTANT.
OKAY.
TRUST IS VERY IMPORTANT.

153
00:11:09,937 --> 00:11:13,273
REASON NUMBER TWO:
WE ARE BOTH 18
AND HAVE NEVER DONE IT.

154
00:11:13,306 --> 00:11:15,275
VERY IMPORTANT !

155
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:18,111
OKAY.
REASON NUMBER THREE:

156
00:11:18,145 --> 00:11:21,414
WE BOTH WANT TO DO IT.

157
00:11:21,448 --> 00:11:24,284
REASON NUMBER FOUR:

158
00:11:26,086 --> 00:11:28,789
PLEASE, LUCY, COME ON.
PLEASE.

159
00:11:28,822 --> 00:11:32,459
I'M, I'M BEGGING YOU.
PLEASE, LET'S JUST DO IT.

160
00:11:32,492 --> 00:11:36,329
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.
YEAH, WE CAN DO IT.
YEAH ?

161
00:11:36,363 --> 00:11:40,000
OKAY, SO LET'S--

162
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:45,105
I'LL GO THIS WAY.
OKAY,
I'M GOING THIS WAY.

163
00:11:45,138 --> 00:11:47,007
LET'S DO THIS.

164
00:11:50,310 --> 00:11:55,082
[ Giggling ]
PLEASE DON'T LAUGH.
YOU'RE KILLING THIS.

165
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:58,819
NO, DON'T YOU WANT YOUR
FIRST TIME TO BE SPECIAL ?
YEAH, THIS IS SPECIAL !

166
00:11:58,852 --> 00:12:01,855
LISTEN, DO YOU WANT TO SPEND
THE REST OF YOUR LIFE...

167
00:12:01,889 --> 00:12:04,391
KNOWING THAT YOU DID IT
FOR THE FIRST TIME
WITH YOUR LAB PARTNER ?

168
00:12:04,424 --> 00:12:07,227
YES, YES, I DO.
AND I'LL TELL YOU WHY.

169
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:10,764
BECAUSE YOU KNOW WHAT IT'S LIKE
FOR A GUY TO GO TO COLLEGE
A VIRGIN ?

170
00:12:10,798 --> 00:12:13,100
HENRY.
NO, I'M TELLING YOU
THEY, THEY--

171
00:12:13,133 --> 00:12:16,837
THEY'RE OSTRACIZED !
THEY TREAT THEM LIKE LEPERS !

172
00:12:16,870 --> 00:12:19,239
I'M SORRY.

173
00:12:19,272 --> 00:12:24,077
WHAT'S UP, MIMI,
HOW'S THE FETUS ?
DROP DEAD.

174
00:12:24,111 --> 00:12:27,547
LOOK, IS IT MINE OR WHAT ?
I CAN'T EVEN BELIEVE
I WENT OUT WITH YOU.

175
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:31,151
I'M TRYING TO DO
THE RIGHT THING HERE.
YEAH ? WHAT'S THE RIGHT THING ?

176
00:12:31,184 --> 00:12:33,420
IGNORING ME
FOR THE PAST FIVE MONTHS ?

177
00:12:33,453 --> 00:12:37,224
LETTING YOUR STUPID FRIENDS
CALL ME A HO ?
SPREADING RUMORS ABOUT ME ?

178
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:43,330
I'M ONLY REPEATIN' WHAT I HEARD:
YOU LET SOME GUY DO YOU
IN HIS CAR OVER CHRISTMAS BREAK.

179
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:47,935
JERK.

180
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:54,541
IT'S TEN PACES
ON THE OTHER SIDE.

181
00:12:56,176 --> 00:12:59,279
- WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE ?
- WHERE'S LUCY ?

182
00:12:59,312 --> 00:13:02,549
SHE'S NOT COMIN'.

183
00:13:02,582 --> 00:13:06,954
YOU HAVE A FLASHLIGHT ?
GOOD.
GIMME BACK MY FLASHLIGHT !

184
00:13:08,355 --> 00:13:12,525
GIMME BACK MY FLASHLIGHT.

185
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:21,101
LET'S JUST GET THIS
OVER WITH, OKAY ?

186
00:13:35,215 --> 00:13:39,452
GOD, I DON'T EVEN REMEMBER
WHAT WE PUT IN HERE.

187
00:13:39,486 --> 00:13:41,454
ME EITHER.

188
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:44,992
HERE, HOLD THIS
FOR A SECOND, LUCY.
WOW.

189
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:54,601
[ Laughing ]

190
00:13:56,636 --> 00:13:59,339
[ Gasps ]
MY BRIDAL BARBIE !

191
00:13:59,372 --> 00:14:02,142
SHE WAS MY WISH.

192
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:04,978
- LOOKS LIKE
YOU'RE GETTIN' YOUR WISH.
- I KNOW.

193
00:14:06,914 --> 00:14:09,349
LUCY, I THINK
THIS IS YOURS.

194
00:14:09,382 --> 00:14:11,484
MY LOCKET.
WHAT DID YOU WISH FOR ?

195
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:16,523
- I-I WANTED TO FIND MY MOM,
TO SEE HER AGAIN.
- DID YOU EVER FIND HER ?

196
00:14:16,556 --> 00:14:21,861
NO, SHE LIVES IN ARIZONA
AND MY POP-- HE DOESN'T THINK
IT'S A GOOD IDEA.

197
00:14:23,463 --> 00:14:26,967
WHAT DID YOU WISH FOR ?

198
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,668
[ Kit Laughs ]

199
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:32,005
- A KEY CHAIN ?
- NO, THE WORLD.

200
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:35,909
THAT I WAS GONNA GET OUT
OF THIS CRAPPY TOWN,

201
00:14:35,943 --> 00:14:38,278
GO ALL THE WAY TO CALIFORNIA,

202
00:14:38,311 --> 00:14:42,950
PUT MY FEET
IN THE PACIFIC OCEAN.

203
00:14:42,983 --> 00:14:45,986
THERE'S A WISH THAT'S NOT
COMING TRUE FOR A WHILE.

204
00:14:46,019 --> 00:14:50,090
- A LOT YOU KNOW, KIT.
- WHAT'S THAT SUPPOSED TO MEAN ?

205
00:14:55,295 --> 00:14:57,464
[ Kit ]
SLIDE RECORDS
RECORDING CONTEST ?

206
00:14:57,497 --> 00:15:01,368
SO ?
SO I'M GOING ON SUNDAY.

207
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:05,638
YOU'RE GOING TO CALIFORNIA
TO AUDITION FOR
A RECORD COMPANY ?

208
00:15:05,672 --> 00:15:08,675
YEAH.
YOU'RE PREGNANT.

209
00:15:08,708 --> 00:15:11,544
SO ? I'LL WEAR
SOMETHING SLIMMING.
AND WHAT ?

210
00:15:11,578 --> 00:15:14,047
YOU THINK YOU'RE GONNA
BECOME THIS BIG, FAT,
PREGNANT STAR ?

211
00:15:14,081 --> 00:15:17,985
- I HAVE A PRETTY GOOD VOICE.
- HOW ARE YOU GONNA GET THERE ?

212
00:15:18,018 --> 00:15:22,055
- I FOUND A RIDE WITH THIS GUY.
- WHAT ? NO, THAT IS CRAZY.

213
00:15:22,089 --> 00:15:25,058
YOU CAN'T GO ALL THE WAY
TO LOS ANGELES BY YOURSELF
WITH SOME GUY.

214
00:15:25,092 --> 00:15:29,729
SO ? THEN COME WITH ME.
I'LL SING LEAD
AND YOU GUYS CAN SING BACKUPS.

215
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:32,732
- I JUST DON'T THINK
THAT'S SOMETHING WE SHOULD DO.
- IT'S STUPID IS WHAT IT IS.

216
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:35,635
OKAY, FINE.
YOU KNOW WHAT ?

217
00:15:35,668 --> 00:15:38,471
YOU CAN JUST FORGET
ALL YOUR PAST !

218
00:15:41,208 --> 00:15:43,110
OH, WOW.

219
00:15:44,711 --> 00:15:49,049
OH, MY GOODNESS.
LOOK AT US !
LET ME SEE.

220
00:15:49,082 --> 00:15:52,085
[ Mimi ]
I WAS SO CHUBBY. SINGING.

221
00:15:54,621 --> 00:15:58,591
- I GOTTA GO NOW.
I HAVE TO GO MEET MY FRIENDS.
- YEAH, IT'S GETTING LATE.

222
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:05,165
YEAH.
HEY, YOU GUYS.

223
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:11,504
I'M LEAVING SUNDAY
AT 7:00 A.M.
IF YOU ALL WANNA COME.

224
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:21,748
[ Kit ]
WHAT DO YOU MEAN YOU'RE NOT
COMING HOME FOR THE SUMMER ?

225
00:16:21,781 --> 00:16:24,717
DYLAN, LISTEN TO ME,
YOU HAVE TO COME HOME.

226
00:16:24,751 --> 00:16:28,688
BECAUSE ! I HAVEN'T SEEN YOU
SINCE CHRISTMAS.

227
00:16:28,721 --> 00:16:30,623
DON'T YOU MISS ME ?

228
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:34,627
- EXCUSE ME.
- DAD, CUSTOMER !

229
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:37,064
DYLAN, WE HAVE TO PLAN
THE WEDDING.

230
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:38,731
[ Clears Throat ]
ALL RIGHT.

231
00:16:38,765 --> 00:16:42,269
I LOVE YOU--
DYLAN ?

232
00:16:46,406 --> 00:16:48,308
HI, JAMIE.

233
00:16:51,811 --> 00:16:54,714
HEY, DARLIN'.
HEY, POP.

234
00:16:54,747 --> 00:16:58,285
DR. JOHNSON CALLED TODAY.
GOOD NEWS.

235
00:16:58,318 --> 00:17:03,223
GOT ME A JOB AT THE HOSPITAL ?
ALL THOSE DISCOUNTS
I GAVE HIM FINALLY PAID OFF.

236
00:17:03,256 --> 00:17:05,492
COOL.
YEP.

237
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:08,528
CAN I ASK YOU A QUESTION ?
MM-HMM.

238
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:11,298
IT'S ABOUT MOTHER.

239
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:14,801
OKAY.

240
00:17:14,834 --> 00:17:18,671
HAD SHE EVER TRIED
TO SEE ME ?
NO, SHE HASN'T.

241
00:17:18,705 --> 00:17:21,608
I WAS THINKING,
MAYBE SHE'S AFRAID TO VISIT ME.

242
00:17:21,641 --> 00:17:25,345
LUCE, WE'VE TALKED ABOUT THIS.
YOU DO NOT HAVE TO FEEL GUILT
ABOUT YOUR MOTHER LEAVING US.

243
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:29,082
BUT WHAT IF WE--
BABY,
THIS IS NOT ABOUT US.

244
00:17:29,116 --> 00:17:32,252
SHE WAS THE ONE
WHO WALKED OUT
ON A THREE-YEAR-OLD.

245
00:17:32,285 --> 00:17:36,123
SHE'S THE ONE
THAT SHOULD FEEL GUILTY.
ALL RIGHT ?

246
00:17:36,156 --> 00:17:38,191
ALL RIGHT.

247
00:18:38,351 --> 00:18:40,420
NOBODY BRINGS FOUR
SUITCASES ON A ROAD TRIP.

248
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:43,856
LOOK, DYLAN ASKED ME
TO GO SEE HIM IN L.A...

249
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:46,626
AND I CAN'T GET THERE
LOOKING LIKE A SKANK.

250
00:18:46,659 --> 00:18:49,362
YOU BETTER HOPE IT ALL FITS.

251
00:18:49,396 --> 00:18:51,398
IT WILL, OKAY ?
HEY.

252
00:18:51,431 --> 00:18:53,333
OH.
HEY.

253
00:18:54,734 --> 00:18:58,571
I'M NOT GOING TO THE AUDITION.
YOU CAN DROP ME OFF IN ARIZONA.

254
00:18:58,605 --> 00:19:01,174
- FINE.
- FINE.

255
00:19:01,208 --> 00:19:05,312
FINE. SHOTGUN.
YEAH, RIGHT.
I'M SITTING UP FRONT.

256
00:19:07,447 --> 00:19:09,916
YOU MUST BE LUCY.

257
00:19:09,949 --> 00:19:12,785
YEAH.

258
00:19:14,354 --> 00:19:16,523
SO YOU'RE TAKING US
TO L.A. ?

259
00:19:16,556 --> 00:19:18,925
UH, YEAH.
I'LL GET YOUR BAG.

260
00:19:20,893 --> 00:19:23,830
YOU OKAY ? ALL RIGHT.
SORRY.
YEAH, I'M FINE.

261
00:19:23,863 --> 00:19:28,368
- MOVE IT, BEN !
LET'S GO ALREADY !
- I'LL GET THE DOOR FOR YOU.

262
00:19:34,707 --> 00:19:36,576
[ Whispering ]
HEY, WHO'S THE GUY ?

263
00:19:36,609 --> 00:19:40,213
THAT'S JUST BEN.
HE'S REALLY COOL.

264
00:19:41,814 --> 00:19:44,351
[ Ben ]
LET'S HIT IT.

265
00:19:51,758 --> 00:19:55,362
* KISS ME
ON THE WAY UP *

266
00:19:55,395 --> 00:19:57,830
* KICK ME
WHEN I FALL DOWN *

267
00:19:57,864 --> 00:20:01,968
* UNDER THE RADAR

268
00:20:02,001 --> 00:20:06,473
* STICK ME IN
THE LOST AND FOUND-- **

269
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:19,552
[ Lucy ]
WHERE'S THE BATHROOM ?

270
00:20:19,586 --> 00:20:22,955
[ Attendant ]
SECOND DOOR.
THERE'S NO SOAP.

271
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:35,735
SO WHAT'S THE DEAL
WITH LUCY ?

272
00:20:35,768 --> 00:20:39,238
WHAT, ARE YOU HOT
FOR HER ?
UH, NO.

273
00:20:40,773 --> 00:20:44,811
I WOULDN'T EVEN TRY, BEN.
SERIOUSLY,
SHE'S NOT LIKE US.

274
00:20:44,844 --> 00:20:46,913
SHE'S WAY OUT
OF YOUR LEAGUE.

275
00:20:50,717 --> 00:20:52,985
WANT A CHIP ?

276
00:20:54,787 --> 00:20:56,889
GET OUTTA HERE.

277
00:21:00,627 --> 00:21:04,931
** [ Radio: Hard Rock ]

278
00:21:04,964 --> 00:21:07,800
** [ Rock ]
WHAT ARE YOU DOIN' ?

279
00:21:07,834 --> 00:21:10,437
WHAT'S WITH THIS MUSIC ?
WELL, I LIKE IT.

280
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:13,005
CAN WE LISTEN TO SOMETHING ELSE
FOR TEN MINUTES ?

281
00:21:13,039 --> 00:21:15,508
NO.

282
00:21:15,542 --> 00:21:19,346
- COME ON, BEN, PLEASE ?
- BE A NICE GUY.

283
00:21:19,379 --> 00:21:22,415
OKAY, FIVE MINUTES.
JUST FIVE MINUTES.

284
00:21:22,449 --> 00:21:25,718
THANK YOU.

285
00:21:25,752 --> 00:21:29,822
* I DON'T WANNA BE
A FOOL *

286
00:21:29,856 --> 00:21:32,892
* IN THIS GAME FOR TWO

287
00:21:32,925 --> 00:21:36,996
* SO I'M LEAVING YOU
BEHIND *

288
00:21:37,029 --> 00:21:40,867
* BYE, BYE, BYE
DON'T MAKE IT TOUGH *

289
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:43,736
* I'VE HAD ENOUGH

290
00:21:43,770 --> 00:21:46,839
* BYE, BYE

291
00:21:46,873 --> 00:21:49,609
* BABY *

292
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:51,944
[ Changes Channels ]

293
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:55,415
- BEN !
- I CAN'T LISTEN TO THIS.

294
00:21:55,448 --> 00:21:57,784
- YOU SAID FIVE MINUTES.
- FORGET IT.

295
00:21:57,817 --> 00:22:00,587
LIKE THIS IS ANY BETTER.

296
00:22:14,501 --> 00:22:17,970
WHY ARE WE STOPPED ?
I'M TIRED.

297
00:22:18,004 --> 00:22:19,806
LET SOMEONE ELSE DRIVE.

298
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:22,475
NO, NOBODY DRIVES
THE CRUISER BUT ME.

299
00:22:22,509 --> 00:22:25,712
- OKAY, WHATEVER.
- WHERE ARE WE GONNA SLEEP ?

300
00:22:25,745 --> 00:22:31,684
THERE'S A FIELD OVER THERE.
I GOT A TENT AND SLEEPING BAGS
IN THE TRUNK.

301
00:22:31,718 --> 00:22:33,953
A, A FIELD ?

302
00:22:33,986 --> 00:22:36,155
NO, I DON'T SLEEP
IN A FIELD.

303
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,858
I SAW A SIGN FOR A HILTON
BACK THERE.

304
00:22:38,891 --> 00:22:41,628
HOW MUCH MONEY
DO WE HAVE ?

305
00:22:44,096 --> 00:22:48,601
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU ONLY BROUGHT $40.

306
00:22:48,635 --> 00:22:53,740
WELL, I HAVE EXPENSES.
I HAD TO HAVE MY
HOMECOMING DRESS CUSTOM-MADE.

307
00:22:53,773 --> 00:22:55,942
I WAS VOTED QUEEN,
YOU KNOW.

308
00:22:55,975 --> 00:22:58,611
OH, MY DREAM COME TRUE.

309
00:22:58,645 --> 00:23:02,415
- DID ANYBODY MAKE A PLAN ?
- WHAT DO YOU MEAN ?

310
00:23:02,449 --> 00:23:05,685
LIKE HOW MANY MILES YOU'RE GONNA
DRIVE IN A DAY ? WHICH TOWNS
YOU'RE GONNA STOP IN ?

311
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:09,622
HOW MUCH GAS MONEY
YOU'RE GONNA NEED ?

312
00:23:09,656 --> 00:23:11,458
OKAY.

313
00:23:11,491 --> 00:23:16,062
WE HAVE $486, RIGHT ?
WHICH MEANS...

314
00:23:16,095 --> 00:23:19,599
FOR FOOD, GAS--

315
00:23:19,632 --> 00:23:21,167
OKAY.

316
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:25,605
- IS IT ENOUGH ?
- IT'S GONNA BE TIGHT.

317
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:31,911
[ Laughs ]
OH, MY GOSH.

318
00:23:31,944 --> 00:23:35,014
IT'S A LOVE ROOM.

319
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:38,017
[ Ben Laughs ]
OH, MAN !

320
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:40,753
LOOK AT THE WALLS !
I'M NOT SLEEPING HERE.

321
00:23:40,787 --> 00:23:45,057
THIS IS WHAT WE CAN AFFORD.
WHAT, IS THIS RUN BY THE HOUR ?
I'M NOT SLEEPING HERE.

322
00:23:45,091 --> 00:23:47,527
WHERE YOU GONNA SLEEP ?
I DON'T KNOW.

323
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:51,097
THIS PLACE IS DISGUSTING.
I'LL TAKE THIS BED.

324
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:54,967
- [ Screams ]
- [ Laughing ]

325
00:24:01,207 --> 00:24:04,110
SO HOW COME
YOU'RE GOING TO L.A. ?

326
00:24:07,113 --> 00:24:09,582
MY UNCLE MIGHT HAVE
A JOB FOR ME THERE,

327
00:24:09,616 --> 00:24:14,120
SO I'M GONNA CHECK IT OUT
AND IF I LIKE IT,
I'LL MOVE THERE.

328
00:24:14,153 --> 00:24:17,690
WHAT ABOUT YOUR BAND ?
DON'T YOU HAVE A BAND ?

329
00:24:17,724 --> 00:24:21,227
NO, I WAS JUST FILLING IN
THE OTHER NIGHT.
I DON'T HAVE A BAND.

330
00:24:23,863 --> 00:24:27,233
MIMI SAID THAT SHE DIDN'T
THINK YOU'D COME WITH US
ON THE TRIP.

331
00:24:29,001 --> 00:24:30,970
NEITHER DID I.

332
00:24:31,003 --> 00:24:33,773
YOU SORRY YOU DID ?

333
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:37,710
NOT SO FAR.

334
00:24:37,744 --> 00:24:39,646
[ Chuckles ]

335
00:24:42,615 --> 00:24:45,084
WELL, GOOD NIGHT.

336
00:24:45,117 --> 00:24:47,153
GOOD NIGHT.

337
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:07,273
- [ Flushes Toilet ]
- HEY !

338
00:25:07,306 --> 00:25:10,142
IT'S FREAKIN' COLD !

339
00:25:10,176 --> 00:25:13,079
WE'RE IN HERE.
I'M IN HERE.

340
00:25:13,112 --> 00:25:15,782
I JUST NEED
TO BRUSH MY TEETH.

341
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:26,559
WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?
YOU'RE SO TOUCHY.

342
00:25:26,593 --> 00:25:28,094
MIMI.

343
00:25:28,127 --> 00:25:31,731
MIMI,
HOW DO YOU KNOW BEN ?

344
00:25:31,764 --> 00:25:35,935
JUST FROM AROUND.
GOD, HE'S SO CUTE.
DON'T YOU THINK HE'S CUTE ?

345
00:25:35,968 --> 00:25:40,072
- HE'S ALL RIGHT.
- I JUST CAN'T BELIEVE
HE WAS IN JAIL.

346
00:25:40,106 --> 00:25:44,143
- WHAT ?
- YEAH !
HE LIKE KILLED A GUY.

347
00:25:44,176 --> 00:25:46,913
KIT !
WHAT ?
THAT'S WHAT I HEARD.

348
00:25:46,946 --> 00:25:49,281
EXCUSE ME ?
HE KILLED SOMEBODY ?

349
00:25:49,315 --> 00:25:53,920
NO, HE DID NOT KILL ANYBODY--
I DON'T THINK.
UH-HUH.

350
00:25:53,953 --> 00:25:58,224
MIMI !
OKAY, HE HAD A CAR, HE WAS
COMING TO L.A. DON'T BE UPSET.

351
00:25:58,257 --> 00:26:02,595
I'M ON A ROAD TRIP
WITH A KILLER AND YOU'RE
TELLING ME NOT TO BE UPSET ?

352
00:26:02,629 --> 00:26:05,832
- [ Whispering ]
HE'LL HEAR YOU.
- OH, MY GOD.

353
00:26:07,299 --> 00:26:11,070
** [ Guitar ]

354
00:26:11,103 --> 00:26:13,740
HEY, WHAT'S UP ?

355
00:26:18,244 --> 00:26:20,947
MIMI, DO YOU
KNOW HIM AT ALL ?

356
00:26:20,980 --> 00:26:24,216
HE USED TO HANG OUT
WITH SOME OF THE GUYS
AT THE TRAILER PARK.

357
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,852
[ Chuckles ]

358
00:26:25,885 --> 00:26:28,955
SO HE MAY HAVE KILLED
SOMEONE, OKAY ?

359
00:26:28,988 --> 00:26:33,860
SO WHAT ?
HE DID HIS TIME.
HE PAID HIS DEBT TO SOCIETY.

360
00:26:33,893 --> 00:26:36,362
OH, MY GOD.

361
00:26:41,701 --> 00:26:44,871
HEY !
YOU ALL READY TO GO ?

362
00:26:44,904 --> 00:26:46,706
YEAH.

363
00:26:46,739 --> 00:26:50,843
HEY, YOU WANNA RIDE UP FRONT
WITH ME TODAY ?

364
00:26:50,877 --> 00:26:53,846
NO, THAT'S OKAY.
THE BACKSEAT'S FINE.
IT'S OKAY.

365
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:57,283
I'M GONNA GO CHECK US OUT,
OKAY ?
YEAH.

366
00:26:57,316 --> 00:27:00,119
* HERE IS SOMETHING
YOU CAN'T UNDERSTAND *

367
00:27:00,152 --> 00:27:02,088
* HOW I COULD JUST KILL A MAN

368
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:05,124
* HERE IS SOMETHING
YOU CAN'T UNDERSTAND *

369
00:27:05,157 --> 00:27:08,394
* HOW I COULD JUST KILL A MAN

370
00:27:10,296 --> 00:27:14,133
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
I'LL COME WITH YA.

371
00:27:14,166 --> 00:27:16,368
NO, IT'S OKAY, I'M FINE.

372
00:27:16,402 --> 00:27:20,206
HEY, LUCE, WILL YOU PLEASE
GET ME SOME CHIPS ?
NO, MIMI.

373
00:27:20,239 --> 00:27:22,909
OPEN THE DOOR.

374
00:27:24,877 --> 00:27:27,714
[ Mimi ]
I'LL GET MY OWN CHIPS.

375
00:27:31,417 --> 00:27:34,854
Y'ALL, WAIT FOR ME !

376
00:27:34,887 --> 00:27:37,790
* HERE IS SOMETHING
YOU CAN'T UNDERSTAND *

377
00:27:37,824 --> 00:27:39,826
* HOW I COULD JUST KILL A MAN *

378
00:27:39,859 --> 00:27:44,130
SO WHEN HE CAME HOME
LAST CHRISTMAS, HE PROPOSED.

379
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:46,899
HE'S COMIN' HOME AS SOON
AS HE'S DONE WITH SCHOOL
NEXT SPRING.

380
00:27:46,933 --> 00:27:50,269
YOU'RE SERIOUSLY
GONNA MARRY THAT LOSER ?

381
00:27:50,302 --> 00:27:52,338
YOU DON'T EVEN KNOW HIM.

382
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:55,908
OW.

383
00:27:55,942 --> 00:27:58,745
WHAT'S WRONG ?
NOTHING.
IT JUST KICKED, IS ALL.

384
00:27:58,778 --> 00:28:01,013
CAN I FEEL IT ?
IF YOU WANT.

385
00:28:01,047 --> 00:28:03,282
IT JUST KICKED AGAIN.

386
00:28:03,315 --> 00:28:07,153
- WHAT ABOUT KURT ?
- WHAT ABOUT KURT ?

387
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:10,790
- HE'S THE FATHER, ISN'T HE ?
- YES, KURT'S THE FATHER.

388
00:28:10,823 --> 00:28:14,460
BUT IT WASN'T WORKING OUT,
SO I DUMPED HIM.

389
00:28:14,493 --> 00:28:16,996
YOU'RE GONNA RAISE THIS BABY
ALL BY YOURSELF ?

390
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:21,300
Y'ALL, I'M GONNA GO WAIT
IN THE CAR WITH BEN, ALL RIGHT ?

391
00:28:21,333 --> 00:28:23,435
THAT'S SO TYPICAL OF HER.

392
00:28:23,469 --> 00:28:27,473
SHE'S NOT EVEN THINKIN'
ABOUT HER FUTURE. HOW'S SHE
GONNA GET BY WITH A BABY ?

393
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:30,276
WELL, SHE BROUGHT THIS
UPON HERSELF.

394
00:28:30,309 --> 00:28:33,279
- KIT.
- WHAT ?

395
00:28:40,086 --> 00:28:42,721
[ Line Ringing ]

396
00:28:43,522 --> 00:28:48,294
- HELLO.
- HI, POP.

397
00:28:48,327 --> 00:28:50,963
LUCY, SNEAKING AWAY
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT ?

398
00:28:50,997 --> 00:28:53,365
I'M VERY UPSET WITH YOU.
DR. JOHNSON WENT...

399
00:28:53,399 --> 00:28:55,835
TO A GREAT DEAL OF TROUBLE
TO GET YOU THAT JOB.

400
00:28:55,868 --> 00:28:59,271
I'M SORRY, OKAY ?
SORRY ?

401
00:28:59,305 --> 00:29:03,175
YOU ARE COMING BACK NOW !
AND YOU WILL REGARD THAT
AS A COMMAND !

402
00:29:03,209 --> 00:29:05,111
YOU'RE USUALLY
SO LEVELHEADED...

403
00:29:05,144 --> 00:29:08,514
AND YOU PULL A STUNT
LIKE THIS, I AM
SO SURPRISED AT YOU, GIRL.

404
00:29:08,547 --> 00:29:11,851
YOU WORKED SO HARD.
ARE YOU GONNA START
SLACKING OFF NOW ?

405
00:29:11,884 --> 00:29:14,954
LUCY ! LUCY ?

406
00:29:28,267 --> 00:29:31,838
WHAT ARE YOU WRITING THERE ?

407
00:29:31,871 --> 00:29:34,306
STUFF.

408
00:29:34,340 --> 00:29:36,442
HEY.

409
00:29:38,210 --> 00:29:40,579
ARE YOU MAD AT ME
OR SOMETHING ?

410
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:43,282
WHY WOULD I BE MAD AT YOU ?
I DON'T EVEN KNOW YOU.

411
00:29:43,315 --> 00:29:46,152
[ Clanking Sound ]
OH, MAN !

412
00:29:46,185 --> 00:29:50,489
NO !
OH, NO, IT SOUNDS BAD.

413
00:29:50,522 --> 00:29:53,559
[ Mimi ]
LOOK AT ALL THAT SMOKE.

414
00:30:04,570 --> 00:30:08,574
OW !
[ Gasps ]
WHAT'S WRONG WITH IT, BEN ?

415
00:30:08,607 --> 00:30:12,078
IT'S THE HEAD GASKET,
I THINK.

416
00:30:12,111 --> 00:30:15,447
GIVE ME YOUR SHIRT.
HERE.

417
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:21,220
WHOA, WHOA, WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?
NOBODY TOUCHES THIS EXCEPT
FOR SPECIALISTS AND MYSELF.

418
00:30:21,253 --> 00:30:24,190
BECAUSE IT'S AN ANTIQUE
AND I DON'T WANT PEOPLE TO--

419
00:30:24,223 --> 00:30:28,594
- IT'S YOUR RADIATOR.
- NO, IT'S THE HEAD GASKET.

420
00:30:28,627 --> 00:30:34,433
NO, YOUR RADIATOR'S CRACKED.
WHAT YEAR IT THIS ? '73.

421
00:30:34,466 --> 00:30:38,237
OH, THAT'S LIKE 350,
PLUS LABOR.

422
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:42,108
[ Clapping ]
GREAT ! GREAT !

423
00:30:52,351 --> 00:30:57,156
I'M HUNGRY.
ALL RIGHT, HOW LONG DOES
IT TAKE TO GET A TOW TRUCK ?

424
00:30:57,189 --> 00:31:01,093
BEN'S ONLY BEEN GONE
FOR TWO HOURS, Y'ALL.
I'M SO HUNGRY.

425
00:31:01,127 --> 00:31:05,131
WILL YOU STOP SAYING THAT ?
WE HEARD YOU.
YOU'RE HUNGRY.

426
00:31:05,164 --> 00:31:07,633
SO WHAT ?

427
00:31:11,670 --> 00:31:13,906
WE DON'T HAVE $350.

428
00:31:13,940 --> 00:31:17,977
AND EVEN IF HE GETS A TOW TRUCK,
WE DON'T HAVE ENOUGH MONEY
TO GET THE CAR FIXED.

429
00:31:18,010 --> 00:31:23,115
I'M GONNA BE STUCK HERE IN--
WHERE THE HELL AM I ?
WHERE AM I ?

430
00:31:23,149 --> 00:31:24,383
LOUISIANA.

431
00:31:24,416 --> 00:31:27,686
STUCK IN SOME
BUTT-HOLE TOWN, LOUISIANA.

432
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:30,256
I AM NEVER GONNA GET
TO L.A. TO SEE DYLAN.

433
00:31:30,289 --> 00:31:32,391
HE'S GONNA BE
SO UPSET.

434
00:31:32,424 --> 00:31:33,960
[ Scoffs ]
WHATEVER.

435
00:31:35,161 --> 00:31:36,963
EXCUSE ME ?

436
00:31:36,996 --> 00:31:39,165
COULD YOU BE MORE
SELF-CENTERED ?

437
00:31:41,433 --> 00:31:45,304
- YOU'RE JUST JEALOUS.
- WHAT ?

438
00:31:45,337 --> 00:31:50,042
I'M NOT BLIND, YOU KNOW.
I KNOW HOW GIRLS LIKE YOU
LOOKED AT ME IN SCHOOL.

439
00:31:50,076 --> 00:31:52,578
YOU WOULD'VE GIVEN ANYTHING
TO TRADE PLACES WITH ME.

440
00:31:52,611 --> 00:31:54,680
GIRLS LIKE ME ?

441
00:31:54,713 --> 00:31:58,084
I CAN'T HELP IT IF I'M
POPULAR, SO JUST LAY OFF.

442
00:32:00,386 --> 00:32:02,254
GIRLS LIKE ME ?

443
00:32:02,288 --> 00:32:05,624
I DIDN'T MAKE THE RULES,
MIMI.
IT'S NOT MY FAULT...

444
00:32:05,657 --> 00:32:08,060
EVERYONE THINKS
YOU'RE A TRAILER-TRASH SKEEZE.

445
00:32:09,261 --> 00:32:11,663
- STOP IT !
- DON'T TOUCH ME LIKE THAT !

446
00:32:11,697 --> 00:32:14,366
- GUYS, DON'T !
- YOU'RE PREGNANT !

447
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:16,535
YOU'RE A REDNECK !

448
00:32:16,568 --> 00:32:21,307
- GIRLS ! MIMI ! STOP !
- [ Shouting ]

449
00:32:21,340 --> 00:32:27,113
STOP IT ! STOP !
I'M SO SICK OF THE TWO OF YOU...

450
00:32:27,146 --> 00:32:29,448
BITCHING AND FIGHTING
EVERY DAMN SECOND OF THE DAY !

451
00:32:29,481 --> 00:32:32,718
FOR ONCE,
WOULD YOU JUST SHUT UP ?

452
00:32:32,751 --> 00:32:36,255
I DON'T KNOW WHY THE HELL
I ASKED THE TWO OF YOU
TO COME ON THIS TRIP.

453
00:32:36,288 --> 00:32:38,424
WE DON'T BELONG TOGETHER.

454
00:32:38,457 --> 00:32:41,127
THIS WAS A MISTAKE, OKAY ?

455
00:32:43,395 --> 00:32:47,966
[ Mechanic ]
I'M SORRY, PARTNER,
THAT'S THE BEST I CAN DO.

456
00:32:49,635 --> 00:32:53,539
IT'S A CRACKED RADIATOR.

457
00:32:53,572 --> 00:32:56,775
HE SAID HE'D GET IT READY
BY TOMORROW.

458
00:32:56,808 --> 00:33:00,112
AND HOW ARE WE GONNA GET
THE MONEY TO PAY FOR IT ?

459
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:04,350
I HAVE AN IDEA.

460
00:33:04,383 --> 00:33:06,618
I'M GONNA CALL MY FATHER
AND HAVE HIM COME GET ME.

461
00:33:06,652 --> 00:33:08,654
YOU'RE LEAVING ?

462
00:33:08,687 --> 00:33:11,157
THIS TRIP'S OVER.

463
00:33:11,190 --> 00:33:13,725
WAIT, I HAVE AN IDEA !

464
00:33:13,759 --> 00:33:16,495
YOU KNOW WHAT ?
I'M SICK OF YOUR IDEAS,
MIMI.

465
00:33:16,528 --> 00:33:18,730
I SHOULD'VE KNOWN YOU'D MAKE
A MESS OF THIS TRIP.

466
00:33:18,764 --> 00:33:24,270
IF YOU WANNA RUN HOME TO
YOUR DADDY, THAT IS FINE, BUT
DON'T TRY AND BLAME THIS ON ME.

467
00:33:33,112 --> 00:33:38,417
LUCY, I HAVEN'T ASKED YOU
FOR ANYTHING
IN A REALLY LONG TIME.

468
00:33:38,450 --> 00:33:40,686
BUT I'M GONNA ASK YOU TO STAY.

469
00:33:40,719 --> 00:33:45,624
[ Line Ringing ]
PLEASE HANG UP THE DAMN PHONE
AND JUST STAY WITH US !

470
00:33:45,657 --> 00:33:47,693
[ Kit ]
COME ON, LUCY.

471
00:33:49,295 --> 00:33:52,098
[ Pop ]
HELLO ?

472
00:33:53,732 --> 00:33:57,269
I DO.
I HAVE A REALLY GOOD IDEA.

473
00:33:57,303 --> 00:34:00,339
YEAH, IT BETTER BE GOOD.

474
00:34:17,523 --> 00:34:20,559
OKAY, I HAVE SOMETHING
TO SAY.

475
00:34:20,592 --> 00:34:24,830
I KNOW WE'RE NOT ALL
GETTING ALONG RIGHT NOW,
BUT TONIGHT'S IMPORTANT.

476
00:34:24,863 --> 00:34:27,299
WE REALLY NEED THE MONEY.

477
00:34:27,333 --> 00:34:32,171
SO COULD WE JUST BE CIVIL
AND GET THROUGH THIS ?
OKAY ?

478
00:34:32,204 --> 00:34:34,273
OKAY.

479
00:34:34,306 --> 00:34:36,208
OKAY.

480
00:34:37,209 --> 00:34:40,846
ALL RIGHT !
Y'ALL READY ?

481
00:34:40,879 --> 00:34:42,848
YEAH.

482
00:34:45,617 --> 00:34:48,154
THAT'S CUTE.
THANK YOU.

483
00:34:53,892 --> 00:34:56,728
WAIT.

484
00:34:56,762 --> 00:34:58,697
IT'S ALL THE TIPS WE CAN GET,
RIGHT ?

485
00:34:58,730 --> 00:35:00,399
MM-HMM.
SO ?

486
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:02,634
IF WE WANNA PUT ON A SHOW,
WE HAVE TO BE SEXY.

487
00:35:02,668 --> 00:35:05,671
NOW YOU'RE TALKIN'.

488
00:35:08,340 --> 00:35:12,211
WHATCHA GOT ?
[ Lucy ]
LET ME WEAR THOSE FEATHERS.

489
00:35:12,244 --> 00:35:14,780
[ Man ]
ALL RIGHT, NEXT CONTESTANT'S
A BRAND-NEW ACT.

490
00:35:14,813 --> 00:35:18,417
AND FOR ALL YOU TOURISTS
THAT DON'T KNOW HOW THE RULES
GO IN MY CLUB,

491
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:20,686
HERE IT IS, PLAIN AND SIMPLE.

492
00:35:20,719 --> 00:35:24,523
YOU'RE THE JUDGE.
IF YOU HATE 'EM, TELL 'EM.
IF YOU LIKE 'EM, PAY 'EM.

493
00:35:24,556 --> 00:35:26,825
WE GOT BASKETS GOING AROUND.
PUT THE MONEY IN THERE.

494
00:35:26,858 --> 00:35:30,362
BE LOUD, BE FAIR
AND ABOVE ALL, BE GENEROUS
IF YOU LIKE WHAT YOU HEAR.

495
00:35:30,396 --> 00:35:33,632
SO, COME ON, GIVE 'EM
A WARM WELCOME.

496
00:35:33,665 --> 00:35:35,767
[ Whistles, Cheers ]

497
00:35:53,752 --> 00:35:59,791
**

498
00:35:59,825 --> 00:36:02,228
THEY LOOK YOUNG.
IT'S PAST
THEIR BEDTIME.

499
00:36:09,335 --> 00:36:13,405
