538
00:39:10,749 --> 00:39:15,587
* I LOVE ROCK AND ROLL
SO SOMEONE PUT A DIME
IN THE JUKEBOX, BABY *

539
00:39:15,621 --> 00:39:20,626
* I LOVE ROCK AND ROLL
SO COME AND TAKE THE TIME
AND DANCE WITH ME *

540
00:39:22,027 --> 00:39:26,465
* ROLL, ROLL, ROLL

541
00:39:26,498 --> 00:39:32,003
* I LOVE ROCK AND ROLL
SO COME AND TAKE THE TIME
AND DANCE WITH ME **

542
00:39:32,037 --> 00:39:35,140
[ Cheering ]

543
00:39:50,188 --> 00:39:52,891
NOW.

544
00:39:52,924 --> 00:39:55,527
IT'S SO AMAZING.

545
00:40:09,074 --> 00:40:11,943
LUCY, COME HERE.

546
00:40:14,079 --> 00:40:17,649
- HOW MUCH IS IT ?
- IT'S ENOUGH FOR THE CAR
AND THE TRIP.

547
00:40:17,683 --> 00:40:20,085
PERFECT.

548
00:40:23,054 --> 00:40:25,957
YOU WANNA COME DANCE WITH US ?

549
00:40:25,991 --> 00:40:30,061
UH, NO. I SHOULD GET YOU GUYS
OUTTA HERE BEFORE SOMEBODY
REALIZES YOU'RE UNDERAGE.

550
00:40:30,095 --> 00:40:32,664
COME ON, JUST A
LITTLE BIT LONGER, PLEASE.

551
00:40:32,698 --> 00:40:36,101
ALL RIGHT,
YOU GO AHEAD.
THANK YOU.

552
00:40:39,505 --> 00:40:44,810
HEY, SHE WITH YOU ?
WHAT ?

553
00:40:44,843 --> 00:40:47,846
IS SHE YOUR GIRL ?

554
00:40:47,879 --> 00:40:49,848
NO.

555
00:40:49,881 --> 00:40:52,884
YEAH. WATCH THIS.

556
00:40:52,918 --> 00:40:55,687
* BEND OVER, GIRL
SHOW ME WHAT
YOU WORKIN' WITH *

557
00:40:55,721 --> 00:40:57,589
* SHAKE YA ASS
BUT WATCH YOURSELF *

558
00:40:57,623 --> 00:41:01,026
* SHAKE YA ASS
SHOW ME WHAT
YOU WORKIN' WITH *

559
00:41:01,059 --> 00:41:05,964
* ATTENTION ALL YOU PLAYERS
AND PIMPS RIGHT NOW
IN THE PLACE TO BE-- **

560
00:41:05,997 --> 00:41:07,733
[ Lucy ]
MOVE YOUR HANDS, PLEASE.

561
00:41:09,868 --> 00:41:13,572
WE'RE GONNA GET A LITTLE FREAKY.
HEY, WHAT'S UP, BABY ? COME ON.

562
00:41:13,605 --> 00:41:15,907
- WHAT'S WRONG ?
- WILL YOU STOP IT ?

563
00:41:15,941 --> 00:41:19,110
EXCUSE ME.
HEY, I DON'T THINK
SHE WANTS TO DANCE.

564
00:41:19,144 --> 00:41:22,247
I THINK SHE DOES.
I THINK YOU SHOULD MIND
YOUR OWN BUSINESS, MAN.

565
00:41:22,280 --> 00:41:25,651
- WILL YOU LEAVE ME ALONE ?
- EXCUSE ME. I'M SORRY.
I WASN'T DONE TALKING TO YOU.

566
00:41:25,684 --> 00:41:28,587
AW, MAN !

567
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:31,022
MY NOSE !

568
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:36,762
- LET'S GO.
- MIMI !

569
00:41:40,966 --> 00:41:44,703
- DAMN !
- IS THIS LIVIN' OR WHAT ?

570
00:41:44,736 --> 00:41:48,206
THERE'S A MINI-BAR !

571
00:41:48,239 --> 00:41:52,911
[ Gasps ]
Y'ALL, YOU COULD SWIM
IN THIS BATHTUB !

572
00:41:52,944 --> 00:41:57,215
BEN, I--
LOOK, I'M--

573
00:41:57,248 --> 00:41:59,718
I'M NOT MAD AT YOU
FOR WHAT HAPPENED THERE.
OKAY ?

574
00:41:59,751 --> 00:42:02,621
[ Mimi ]
THERE'S BATHROBES !

575
00:42:02,654 --> 00:42:04,856
WHERE ARE YOU GOING ?
JUST GOING OUT.

576
00:42:04,890 --> 00:42:06,758
OKAY.

577
00:42:06,792 --> 00:42:09,661
ARE ANY OF YOU GUYS TIRED,
'CAUSE IT'S 3:00 A.M.
AND I'M WIRED !

578
00:42:09,695 --> 00:42:15,033
- [ Laughs ] WHO WANTS
SOME OF MAMA'S PUNCH ?
- ME, PLEASE.

579
00:42:15,066 --> 00:42:18,103
MADAME.
MADAME.

580
00:42:21,139 --> 00:42:25,577
** [ Hip-Hop ]
OHH !

581
00:42:25,611 --> 00:42:28,079
WHOO !

582
00:42:28,113 --> 00:42:30,816
YEOW !

583
00:42:37,689 --> 00:42:41,627
GO, LUCY ! GO, LUCY !
WHOO !

584
00:42:45,230 --> 00:42:48,266
WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?

585
00:42:48,299 --> 00:42:52,704
YEOW !
YOU GO, GIRL !

586
00:42:54,973 --> 00:42:56,942
- [ Belches ]
- [ Laughing ]

587
00:42:58,109 --> 00:43:01,012
I HAVE SEEN ONE, Y'ALL.

588
00:43:01,046 --> 00:43:04,850
YEAH, BUT HAVE YOU
TOUCHED ONE ?

589
00:43:06,351 --> 00:43:10,221
SHE HAS !
GIVE US THE DETAILS !

590
00:43:10,255 --> 00:43:13,825
IT'S ALWAYS THE QUIET ONES.

591
00:43:13,859 --> 00:43:16,394
SAY IT LOUD.
SAY YOU TOUCHED ONE
AND YOU'RE PROUD !

592
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:19,665
LUCY TOUCHED ONE !
SHE DID !

593
00:43:29,107 --> 00:43:32,644
[ Lucy ]
OKAY, THE BEST THING
THAT EVER HAPPENED TO YOU.

594
00:43:32,678 --> 00:43:35,981
THAT'S EASY.
WHAT ?

595
00:43:36,014 --> 00:43:38,817
REACHING MY GOAL WEIGHT.

596
00:43:38,850 --> 00:43:42,353
THIRD YEAR AT FAT CAMP,
THE SUMMER BEFORE EIGHTH GRADE.

597
00:43:42,387 --> 00:43:46,157
WAIT, THAT CAMP
YOU WENT TO EVERY SUMMER
WAS A FAT CAMP ?

598
00:43:49,861 --> 00:43:51,997
YES,
AND I LOVED IT.

599
00:43:52,030 --> 00:43:58,670
FOR TWO MONTHS, MY MAMA
WASN'T AROUND TO PICK ON ME
FOR BEING FAT.

600
00:43:59,771 --> 00:44:03,208
BEING FAT IS JUST
UNACCEPTABLE TO HER.

601
00:44:04,910 --> 00:44:08,880
OKAY. THE WORST THING
THAT EVER HAPPENED TO YOU.

602
00:44:08,914 --> 00:44:11,416
THAT'S EVEN EASIER.
REACHING MY GOAL WEIGHT.

603
00:44:11,449 --> 00:44:13,318
YOU JUST SAID--
IT TURNS OUT...

604
00:44:13,351 --> 00:44:17,088
THAT BEING PRETTIER
THAN MY MAMA...

605
00:44:17,122 --> 00:44:19,858
IS EVEN MORE
UNACCEPTABLE.

606
00:44:19,891 --> 00:44:22,694
WOW.
OH, JESUS.

607
00:44:24,095 --> 00:44:26,231
YEP.

608
00:44:26,264 --> 00:44:30,268
[ Lucy ]
ONE MORNING I WOKE UP,
AND SHE WAS GONE.

609
00:44:30,301 --> 00:44:33,138
POP REALLY WOULDN'T
SAY ANYTHING ABOUT IT.

610
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:37,308
I THOUGHT SHE WAS
COMING BACK, AND
POP TOLD ME SHE WASN'T.

611
00:44:37,342 --> 00:44:40,979
THEY FOUGHT ALL THE TIME.

612
00:44:41,012 --> 00:44:44,415
YOU KNOW, I THINK
THAT SHE JUST GOT FED UP...

613
00:44:44,449 --> 00:44:47,152
AND TOOK OFF
WITHOUT EVEN THINKING.

614
00:44:47,185 --> 00:44:51,422
AND AFTER A WHILE,
IT WAS JUST TOO LATE
TO COME BACK.

615
00:44:53,224 --> 00:44:55,861
I KNOW SHE WANTS TO SEE ME.

616
00:44:58,229 --> 00:45:00,799
SHE'S JUST SCARED,
THAT'S ALL.

617
00:45:02,467 --> 00:45:05,971
I'M GONNA BE SO SICK LATER.

618
00:45:06,004 --> 00:45:09,240
MIMI, BE GLAD YOU'RE PREGNANT
AND YOU COULDN'T
ACT STUPID WITH US.

619
00:45:09,274 --> 00:45:14,079
THAT'S NOT WHY I DON'T DRINK.
I JUST DON'T SEE
THE POINT IN IT.

620
00:45:14,112 --> 00:45:15,881
SO YOU NEVER PARTIED ?

621
00:45:18,316 --> 00:45:20,385
ONCE.

622
00:45:22,053 --> 00:45:25,090
UM, OVER CHRISTMAS.

623
00:45:25,123 --> 00:45:28,927
THERE WAS ONE OF THOSE PARTIES
AT HEMMINGS FIELD.

624
00:45:30,528 --> 00:45:33,231
AND THIS GUY WAS DRINKING
THIS BEER,

625
00:45:33,264 --> 00:45:38,169
AND I REMEMBER
IT WAS IN A BLUE BOTTLE.

626
00:45:38,203 --> 00:45:42,040
AND I WAS REAL MAD
AT KURT BECAUSE...

627
00:45:42,073 --> 00:45:46,011
HE BLEW ME OFF AGAIN
TO HANG OUT WITH HIS FRIENDS.

628
00:45:47,412 --> 00:45:50,315
SO I HAD A FEW BEERS.

629
00:45:52,083 --> 00:45:54,385
I HAD MORE THAN A FEW.

630
00:45:56,154 --> 00:45:59,257
THIS GUY, YOU KNOW,
HE SEEMED--

631
00:45:59,290 --> 00:46:03,494
HE SEEMED REAL NICE,
'CAUSE WHEN I COULDN'T WALK,
HE OFFERED TO DRIVE ME HOME.

632
00:46:05,096 --> 00:46:08,133
MIMI.

633
00:46:08,166 --> 00:46:11,402
IT'S NO BIG DEAL, LUCE.
IT HAPPENS TO GIRLS
ALL THE TIME.

634
00:46:11,436 --> 00:46:14,139
[ Lucy ]
DID YOU GO TO THE POLICE ?

635
00:46:14,172 --> 00:46:16,174
NO.

636
00:46:16,207 --> 00:46:19,911
I'M FROM A TRAILER PARK, LUCE.
I GOT DRUNK AND GOT IN HIS CAR.

637
00:46:19,945 --> 00:46:23,114
SO, KU--
SO, KURT'S NOT THE FATHER ?

638
00:46:23,148 --> 00:46:26,551
I SAW THIS AD
IN A MAGAZINE.

639
00:46:26,584 --> 00:46:32,824
SO I CALLED UP THIS LAWYER
OUT IN ATLANTA,
AND SHE SENT ME ALL THIS STUFF.

640
00:46:32,858 --> 00:46:35,260
UM, ALL THESE PICTURES
AND LETTERS...

641
00:46:35,293 --> 00:46:38,196
OF ALL THESE PEOPLE
WHO WANT BABIES.

642
00:46:38,229 --> 00:46:40,999
I WAS SUPPOSED TO PICK ONE.
[ Kit ]
THE GUY,

643
00:46:43,301 --> 00:46:45,570
WHAT WAS HIS NAME ?

644
00:46:47,572 --> 00:46:49,875
I DON'T KNOW.

645
00:46:52,243 --> 00:46:55,847
WHY DID WE STOP
BEING FRIENDS ?

646
00:46:55,881 --> 00:46:58,616
I DON'T KNOW.
PEOPLE DRIFT APART.

647
00:46:58,649 --> 00:47:02,553
WELL, PROMISE ME
WE WON'T DRIFT APART AGAIN.

648
00:47:04,389 --> 00:47:07,525
COME HERE.

649
00:47:07,558 --> 00:47:10,896
AND WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN
ALL NIGHT ?

650
00:47:18,236 --> 00:47:20,238
THANK YOU.

651
00:47:20,271 --> 00:47:22,941
FOR WHAT YOU DID
LAST NIGHT, I MEAN.

652
00:47:22,974 --> 00:47:25,043
THANKS.

653
00:47:27,378 --> 00:47:30,515
SCOOT OVER.

654
00:47:39,457 --> 00:47:44,062
I'M NEVER DRINKIN' AGAIN.
HONEST.
THIS BURRITO IS SO GOOD.

655
00:47:44,095 --> 00:47:46,631
DON'T MENTION FOOD.

656
00:47:47,933 --> 00:47:51,136
WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?
CHILLING.

657
00:47:53,404 --> 00:47:55,907
SHH.

658
00:48:02,147 --> 00:48:05,416
- WAKE HIM UP.
- Y'ALL, HE'S BEEN DRIVING
ALL DAY.

659
00:48:05,450 --> 00:48:09,620
- WE CAN'T JUST STAY HERE.
- WE SHOULD JUST LET HIM SLEEP.

660
00:48:09,654 --> 00:48:12,257
UH-UH.
[ Mimi ]
YEAH, WE'LL LET HIM SLEEP.

661
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:15,693
LUCY, GET HIS KEYS.

662
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:18,529
HE TOLD US WE COULDN'T DRIVE
HIS CAR. I CAN'T DO THAT.

663
00:48:18,563 --> 00:48:21,366
AND WHY NOT ?
IT'S NOT LIKE WE'RE GONNA DRIVE
THIS OVER A CLIFF OR ANYTHING.

664
00:48:21,399 --> 00:48:25,236
AND IT'S STUPID
TO STAY HERE.
[ Mimi ]
I'LL DRIVE.

665
00:48:25,270 --> 00:48:26,637
GET HIS KEYS.

666
00:48:26,671 --> 00:48:29,674
YEAH, GET HIS KEYS.
WHY DO I HAVE
TO GET HIS KEYS ?

667
00:48:29,707 --> 00:48:34,112
BECAUSE KIT AND I VOTED
AND YOU LOST.

668
00:48:34,145 --> 00:48:36,181
LUCY, GET THE KEYS.

669
00:48:36,214 --> 00:48:39,017
YEAH, LUCY,
GET HIS KEYS.

670
00:48:39,050 --> 00:48:41,386
OKAY.

671
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:44,155
[ Squeaking, Bangs Foot ]

672
00:48:44,189 --> 00:48:46,191
SHH, SHH, SHH.

673
00:48:46,224 --> 00:48:50,728
- THIS IS STEALING.
- IT'S NOT STEALING
IF HE'S IN THE CAR WITH US.

674
00:48:50,761 --> 00:48:53,464
NO, IT'S KIDNAPPING.

675
00:48:59,670 --> 00:49:02,507
[ Whispering ]
OKAY, STOP.

676
00:49:02,540 --> 00:49:04,209
OKAY, OKAY.

677
00:49:05,710 --> 00:49:08,613
[ Whispering ]
OH, I GOT IT.

678
00:49:17,655 --> 00:49:20,525
OKAY, GO, GO, GO.

679
00:49:29,100 --> 00:49:31,136
MIMI.

680
00:49:31,169 --> 00:49:34,072
YOU FAILED DRIVER'S ED,
DIDN'T YOU ?

681
00:49:34,105 --> 00:49:36,207
MAYBE.

682
00:49:36,241 --> 00:49:40,011
MOVE OVER.
OH, GOD.

683
00:49:40,778 --> 00:49:43,181
GUYS, SMILE
FOR THE CAMERA.

684
00:49:57,228 --> 00:49:59,630
TURN IT ON, TURN IT ON.

685
00:50:00,831 --> 00:50:02,767
OKAY.

686
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:06,737
** [ Rock ]

687
00:50:06,771 --> 00:50:09,274
* LET'S GO, GIRLS

688
00:50:15,680 --> 00:50:19,617
* I'M GOIN' OUT TONIGHT
AND I'M FEELING ALL RIGHT *

689
00:50:19,650 --> 00:50:23,354
* I'M GONNA LET
IT ALL HANG OUT *

690
00:50:23,388 --> 00:50:27,358
* WANNA MAKE SOME NOISE
REALLY RAISE MY VOICE *

691
00:50:27,392 --> 00:50:31,296
* YEAH, I'M GONNA
SCREAM AND SHOUT *

692
00:50:33,498 --> 00:50:35,800
* AHH

693
00:50:35,833 --> 00:50:39,137
* NO INHIBITIONS
MAKE NO CONDITIONS *

694
00:50:39,170 --> 00:50:42,740
* GET A LITTLE OUTTA LINE

695
00:50:42,773 --> 00:50:46,277
* I AIN'T GONNA ACT
POLITICALLY CORRECT *

696
00:50:46,311 --> 00:50:50,648
* I ONLY WANNA HAVE
A GOOD TIME *

697
00:50:50,681 --> 00:50:54,752
* THE BEST THING ABOUT
BEING A WOMAN *

698
00:50:54,785 --> 00:50:59,124
* IS THE PREROGATIVE
TO HAVE A LITTLE FUN AND *

699
00:50:59,157 --> 00:51:04,695
* OH, OH, OH
GO TOTALLY CRAZY-- **

700
00:51:04,729 --> 00:51:07,832
HI !
DID YOU HAVE A GOOD NAP ?
YEAH.

701
00:51:07,865 --> 00:51:10,168
STOP, STOP THE CAR.

702
00:51:10,201 --> 00:51:13,271
DON'T BE MAD.
YOU LOOKED SO SWEET
WHEN YOU WERE SLEEPING.

703
00:51:13,304 --> 00:51:16,607
- WE JUST DIDN'T WANNA WAKE YOU.
- STOP THE CAR.

704
00:51:16,641 --> 00:51:19,310
- IT'S AGAINST THE LAW
TO PARK ON THE SHOULDER.
- IT'S MY CAR.

705
00:51:19,344 --> 00:51:21,846
- WE'RE ALMOST AT AN EXIT.
- STOP THE DAMN CAR !

706
00:51:21,879 --> 00:51:24,149
** [ Radio Switches Off ]

707
00:51:35,593 --> 00:51:37,195
[ Ben Shouts ]

708
00:51:43,268 --> 00:51:47,205
MIMI, GO TALK TO HIM.
UH-UH,
YOU GO TALK TO HIM.

709
00:51:47,238 --> 00:51:50,141
NOBODY'S GONNA GO
TALK TO HIM.
I KNOW, HE'S MAD.

710
00:51:51,376 --> 00:51:53,678
AND HE HAS KILLED BEFORE.

711
00:51:53,711 --> 00:51:57,282
MIMI, YOU SAID
HE DIDN'T KILL ANYONE.

712
00:51:57,315 --> 00:52:01,419
I SAID I THOUGHT
HE DIDN'T KILL ANYBODY.
OH, MY GOD.

713
00:52:05,890 --> 00:52:08,793
IT'S OKAY, I'LL GO.
I'M SORRY.

714
00:52:12,630 --> 00:52:14,599
GOD !

715
00:52:14,632 --> 00:52:17,468
[ Mimi ]
BE CAREFUL, LUCY.

716
00:52:23,374 --> 00:52:26,744
- WE'RE SORRY.
- I'VE BEEN IN A CAR
FULL OF CHICKS FOR DAYS.

717
00:52:26,777 --> 00:52:30,381
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA WHAT
IT'S LIKE BEING SURROUNDED
BY GIRLS ALL THE TIME ?

718
00:52:30,415 --> 00:52:32,517
OKAY--

719
00:52:32,550 --> 00:52:35,720
BEING A GIRL YOURSELF,
I KNOW, STUPID QUESTION.

720
00:52:35,753 --> 00:52:39,524
BUT I'M A GUY, OKAY ?
I'M A GUY. JUST A GUY.

721
00:52:39,557 --> 00:52:43,928
AND I HAVE BEEN LISTENING
TO NOTHING BUT GIRL TALK
AND WATCHING YOU ALL DO...

722
00:52:43,961 --> 00:52:46,664
YOUR GIRL THINGS FOR DAYS.

723
00:52:46,697 --> 00:52:49,600
AND I'M NOT COMPLAINING,
'CAUSE, LET'S FACE IT,
I'M OUTNUMBERED.

724
00:52:49,634 --> 00:52:51,502
BUT THAT'S MY CAR.

725
00:52:51,536 --> 00:52:56,207
IT'S MY CAR,
AND IT'S JUST--

726
00:52:58,809 --> 00:53:01,446
IT'S THE ONE THING
THAT HASN'T BEEN TAKEN OVER
BY CHICKS.

727
00:53:03,314 --> 00:53:06,851
OKAY ?
OKAY.

728
00:53:10,821 --> 00:53:14,959
* NOBODY REALLY KNOWS

729
00:53:14,992 --> 00:53:19,497
* WHERE THEY'RE SUPPOSED
TO GO *

730
00:53:19,530 --> 00:53:23,268
* HIDING BEHIND THE WALL

731
00:53:23,301 --> 00:53:27,438
* AFRAID THAT THEY'LL
LOSE IT ALL *

732
00:53:27,472 --> 00:53:32,343
* BUT IT'S ALL RIGHT
JUST FOLLOW THE LIGHT *

733
00:53:32,377 --> 00:53:35,980
* AND DON'T BE AFRAID
OF THE DARK **

734
00:53:37,715 --> 00:53:40,885
BEN ?
YEAH ?

735
00:53:40,918 --> 00:53:43,388
WERE YOU REALLY IN JAIL ?

736
00:53:44,489 --> 00:53:47,658
YEAH, I WAS.

737
00:53:47,692 --> 00:53:49,994
SO YOU KILLED A GUY ?
WHAT ?

738
00:53:50,995 --> 00:53:53,364
WHO SAID I KILLED A GUY ?

739
00:53:54,499 --> 00:53:57,702
EVERYBODY BACK HOME.

740
00:53:57,735 --> 00:54:02,507
OH, MAN.
NO, I DIDN'T KILL A GUY.

741
00:54:02,540 --> 00:54:04,609
WHAT DID YOU DO THEN ?

742
00:54:04,642 --> 00:54:07,011
I WAS IN COLLEGE,

743
00:54:07,044 --> 00:54:10,448
AND I GET THIS CALL
FROM MY STEPSISTER.

744
00:54:10,481 --> 00:54:15,753
SHE WANTS ME TO COME HOME
AND GET HER 'CAUSE MY STEPDAD
IS BEATING HER UP PRETTY BAD.

745
00:54:15,786 --> 00:54:17,755
MY MOM CAN'T STOP HIM,
SO...

746
00:54:17,788 --> 00:54:20,391
YEAH, I DRIVE HOME
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT,

747
00:54:20,425 --> 00:54:24,995
AND SHE THROWS HER THINGS OUT
THE WINDOW AND CLIMBS OUT,

748
00:54:25,029 --> 00:54:27,031
AND THEN I DRIVE HER BACK
TO SCHOOL IN OHIO WITH ME.

749
00:54:27,064 --> 00:54:30,668
AND YOU WENT TO JAIL
FOR THAT ?
THAT'S THE THING.

750
00:54:30,701 --> 00:54:36,307
THERE'S THIS LAW AGAINST DRIVING
A CHILD THAT'S NOT A RELATIVE
ACROSS STATE LINES,

751
00:54:36,341 --> 00:54:38,509
AND MY STEPDAD OF COURSE
PRESSED CHARGES.

752
00:54:38,543 --> 00:54:41,812
BUT, YOU KNOW, IT'S OKAY.
I ONLY GOT SIX MONTHS,

753
00:54:41,846 --> 00:54:44,349
AND THEN I HAD
TO STAY IN OHIO
FOR A YEAR'S PROBATION.

754
00:54:44,382 --> 00:54:47,952
AND MY SISTER GOT TO GO LIVE
WITH HER MOM.

755
00:54:53,791 --> 00:54:56,461
YOU ALL REALLY THOUGHT
I KILLED A GUY ?

756
00:54:56,494 --> 00:54:58,429
YEAH.

757
00:55:01,098 --> 00:55:05,570
WHAT IN THE HELL WERE
YOU THINKING GETTING INTO
A CAR WITH A HOMICIDAL MANIAC ?

758
00:55:07,705 --> 00:55:09,940
HUH ?

759
00:55:11,642 --> 00:55:13,544
MAN.

760
00:55:15,980 --> 00:55:20,585
* I NEVER MINDED
GIVING US THE STARS *

761
00:55:22,553 --> 00:55:25,823
[ Mimi ]
WHY ARE WE STOPPING ?
[ Ben ] YOU'LL SEE.

762
00:55:25,856 --> 00:55:30,661
* YOU PAINTED ME A PICTURE
AND SHOWED ME HOW TO SEE *

763
00:55:30,695 --> 00:55:37,568
* BUT I JUST WON'T BEHOLD IT
UNLESS IT PERTAINS TO ME-- **

764
00:55:37,602 --> 00:55:40,971
MIMI, YOU OKAY ?
OH, YEAH, I'M FINE.

765
00:55:45,476 --> 00:55:47,478
LOOK.

766
00:55:47,512 --> 00:55:49,480
[ Lucy ]
WOW.

767
00:55:50,815 --> 00:55:54,118
IT'S LIKE YOU HAVE
TO WHISPER.

768
00:55:55,853 --> 00:55:57,888
HELLO !

769
00:55:59,023 --> 00:56:01,592
- HELLO !
- HELLO !

770
00:56:01,626 --> 00:56:03,628
HELLO !

771
00:56:06,997 --> 00:56:10,701
OH, MAN. WE GOTTA MAKE TIME.
THE NEXT HOTEL IS STILL
AN HOUR AWAY.

772
00:56:10,735 --> 00:56:14,739
WELL, BEN, DO YOU HAVE
ENOUGH SLEEPING BAGS
FOR ALL OF US ?

773
00:56:14,772 --> 00:56:16,741
ARE YOU SERIOUS ?

774
00:56:16,774 --> 00:56:20,911
Y'ALL, YOU REALLY WANT
TO CAMP HERE ?
YEAH.

775
00:56:20,945 --> 00:56:22,913
YEAH.

776
00:56:22,947 --> 00:56:25,015
IT SOUNDS LIKE FUN.

777
00:56:26,617 --> 00:56:31,388
[ Mimi ]
YOU GOTTA KEEP YOUR THUMB
ON THE OUTSIDE LIKE THIS.

778
00:56:32,723 --> 00:56:34,892
RIGHT. NOW, THE TRICK IS...

779
00:56:34,925 --> 00:56:38,663
YOU DON'T WANT TO LET HIM KNOW
THAT YOU'RE GONNA HIT HIM.

780
00:56:38,696 --> 00:56:42,700
MAYBE LIKE LOOK AWAY FIRST.

781
00:56:42,733 --> 00:56:46,637
AND THEN, WHEN HE LEAST
EXPECTS IT, YOU THROW
YOUR WHOLE BODY INTO IT.

782
00:56:46,671 --> 00:56:48,172
OKAY.

783
00:56:50,207 --> 00:56:53,143
[ Laughing ]
MIMI, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING TO HER ?

784
00:56:53,177 --> 00:56:55,079
I'M TEACHING HER HOW TO
FIGHT BECAUSE EVERY GIRL...

785
00:56:55,112 --> 00:56:57,782
SHOULD KNOW HOW
TO THROW A DECENT PUNCH.

786
00:56:57,815 --> 00:56:59,784
THAT WAS DECENT.

787
00:56:59,817 --> 00:57:01,652
I'M GONNA GO TO BED.

788
00:57:01,686 --> 00:57:04,555
I'M GONNA GO
TO THE LADIES ROOM.
WHERE IS IT AGAIN ?

789
00:57:04,589 --> 00:57:07,758
THIRD BUSH AFTER THE ROCK
OVER THERE.

790
00:57:07,792 --> 00:57:10,127
THIS ONE ?
THAT ONE, YEAH.

791
00:57:15,032 --> 00:57:17,167
OKAY, WHAT ARE YOU ALWAYS
WRITING IN THERE ?

792
00:57:18,736 --> 00:57:21,672
POEMS, MOSTLY.

793
00:57:21,706 --> 00:57:25,476
CAN I HEAR ONE ?

794
00:57:25,510 --> 00:57:29,446
OKAY. ONE.
BUT YOU CAN'T LAUGH.

795
00:57:30,915 --> 00:57:34,519
OKAY.

796
00:57:34,552 --> 00:57:37,187
"I USED TO THINK I HAD
THE ANSWERS TO EVERYTHING,

797
00:57:37,221 --> 00:57:39,690
"BUT NOW I KNOW THAT LIFE
DOESN'T ALWAYS GO MY WAY.

798
00:57:39,724 --> 00:57:42,092
"IT FEELS LIKE I'M CAUGHT
IN THE MIDDLE.

799
00:57:42,126 --> 00:57:47,164
"AND THAT'S WHEN I REALIZE
THAT I'M NOT A GIRL,
AND NOT YET A WOMAN.

800
00:57:47,197 --> 00:57:51,135
"ALL I NEED IS TIME,
JUST A MOMENT THAT'S MINE.

801
00:57:51,168 --> 00:57:54,605
AND WHILE I'M IN BETWEEN,
I'M NOT A GIRL."

802
00:57:58,042 --> 00:58:00,578
I LIKED IT.

803
00:58:00,611 --> 00:58:02,012
REALLY ?

804
00:58:02,046 --> 00:58:04,481
YEAH, REALLY,
I LIKED IT.

805
00:58:08,786 --> 00:58:12,222
WHAT ?
WELL, YOU GOT ASH
ON YOUR FACE.

806
00:58:12,256 --> 00:58:14,625
WHERE ?
I'LL GET IT.

807
00:58:14,659 --> 00:58:16,561
THERE.

808
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:25,235
[ Screaming ]

809
00:58:25,269 --> 00:58:27,037
- WHAT'S WRONG ?
- WHAT HAPPENED ?

810
00:58:27,071 --> 00:58:29,540
SOMETHING BIT MY ASS.

811
00:58:29,574 --> 00:58:32,610
LET ME SEE.
IT'S A SNAKE BITE.

812
00:58:32,643 --> 00:58:34,712
NO, REALLY,
THAT'S A MOSQUITO BITE.

813
00:58:34,745 --> 00:58:36,747
[ Both ]
OW !

814
00:58:36,781 --> 00:58:38,616
MIMI--
DON'T LOOK !

815
00:58:38,649 --> 00:58:41,886
HOW COULD I NOT ?
IT'S NOTHING.
BUT IT COULD'VE BEEN A SNAKE.

816
00:58:41,919 --> 00:58:44,955
ALL RIGHT ! WE ARE
OUTTA HERE AT THE CRACK OF DAWN.

817
00:58:44,989 --> 00:58:49,093
NOTHING'S BITING MY ASS.

818
00:58:49,126 --> 00:58:52,296
[ Lucy ]
SO WE'LL BE IN TUCSON TODAY ?

819
00:58:52,329 --> 00:58:55,165
AROUND 4:00, I THINK.
[ Ben ]
ARE YOU NERVOUS ?

820
00:58:55,199 --> 00:58:59,069
SHOULD I CALL AND TELL HER
THAT I'M COMING,
OR SHOULD I JUST SHOW UP ?

821
00:58:59,103 --> 00:59:02,339
I SHOULD JUST SHOW UP,
RIGHT ?
SURPRISE IS ALWAYS BETTER.

822
00:59:02,372 --> 00:59:05,843
SHE'S GONNA BE REAL HAPPY
TO SEE YOU.

823
00:59:05,876 --> 00:59:08,545
[ Lucy ]
I HOPE SO.

824
00:59:16,153 --> 00:59:19,089
[ Mimi ]
WHOA.

825
00:59:21,025 --> 00:59:24,729
OKAY, SO YOU'RE GONNA CALL ME
AND TELL ME EVERYTHING
ABOUT THE AUDITION, RIGHT ?

826
00:59:24,762 --> 00:59:29,066
YOU COULD STILL COME WITH US.
WE'RE NOT LEAVING TOWN
UNTIL TOMORROW.

827
00:59:29,099 --> 00:59:31,068
I'LL BE FINE, OKAY ?

828
00:59:31,101 --> 00:59:34,639
[ Mimi ]
YOU KNOW WHERE WE'RE STAYING
IF YOU NEED US.

829
00:59:35,740 --> 00:59:37,842
BYE.

830
00:59:41,211 --> 00:59:43,948
THANKS.
YEAH.

831
00:59:43,981 --> 00:59:46,216
I GUESS THIS IS IT.

832
00:59:48,986 --> 00:59:50,988
I GUESS, YEAH.

833
00:59:51,021 --> 00:59:53,123
WHAT ?

834
00:59:58,996 --> 01:00:00,965
GOOD LUCK.

835
01:00:00,998 --> 01:00:02,900
THANKS.

836
01:00:09,006 --> 01:00:10,875
[ Doorbell Rings ]

837
01:00:13,277 --> 01:00:15,279
CAN I HELP YOU ?

838
01:00:15,312 --> 01:00:18,615
IT'S ME, MAMA-- LUCY.

839
01:00:20,885 --> 01:00:22,820
COME IN.

840
01:00:35,966 --> 01:00:40,237
YOU HAVE
A REALLY NICE HOUSE.
THANK YOU... LUCY.

841
01:00:54,184 --> 01:00:56,687
TUCSON SEEMS LIKE
A REALLY NICE CITY.

842
01:00:56,721 --> 01:00:58,789
IT IS.

843
01:00:58,823 --> 01:01:03,260
CAN I, UH, ASK YOU WHY
YOU'RE HERE... LUCY ?

844
01:01:04,829 --> 01:01:06,864
I WANTED TO SEE YOU.

845
01:01:06,897 --> 01:01:08,866
AND WHY WAS THAT, LUCY ?

846
01:01:11,068 --> 01:01:13,403
WELL, YOU'RE MY MOTHER.

847
01:01:20,344 --> 01:01:24,314
LUCY--
WHY DO YOU KEEP
SAYING MY NAME LIKE THAT ?

848
01:01:24,348 --> 01:01:26,851
[ Phone Rings ]

849
01:01:30,320 --> 01:01:32,689
HOLD ON A MOMENT.

850
01:01:40,230 --> 01:01:41,932
HELLO ?

851
01:01:41,966 --> 01:01:47,071
SWEETIE, TELL JOEY'S MOMMY I
SAID YOU COULD SWIM FOR ANOTHER
HOUR IF YOU PUT ON SUNSCREEN.

852
01:01:47,104 --> 01:01:48,939
[ Continues, Indistinct ]

853
01:01:48,973 --> 01:01:52,342
DADDY WILL PICK YOU UP AT 5:00.
I LOVE YOU.

854
01:02:01,218 --> 01:02:05,823
I HAVE BROTHERS ?
WELL, YES.

855
01:02:05,856 --> 01:02:10,060
HOW OLD ARE THEY ?
TEN AND SEVEN.

856
01:02:12,062 --> 01:02:13,964
DO THEY KNOW ABOUT ME ?

857
01:02:17,234 --> 01:02:21,405
LUCY, I THINK WE NEED
TO HAVE A TALK.

858
01:02:23,007 --> 01:02:24,875
[ Thunder Rumbles ]

859
01:02:26,410 --> 01:02:29,346
* WHOA
WAIT, SEVEN, EIGHT.

860
01:02:29,379 --> 01:02:31,448
FIVE, SIX--

861
01:02:37,387 --> 01:02:40,991
[ Knock At Door ]

862
01:02:44,929 --> 01:02:46,763
LUCY.

863
01:02:48,532 --> 01:02:50,534
COME ON IN. HERE.

864
01:02:50,567 --> 01:02:52,469
WHAT HAPPENED ?
WHAT'S WRONG ?

865
01:02:52,502 --> 01:02:54,438
GET SOME TOWELS.
I'M FINE.

866
01:02:54,471 --> 01:02:57,808
SO, LUCE, YOU GOT TO SEE
YOUR MOM, RIGHT ?

867
01:02:57,842 --> 01:03:02,112
- YEAH, I SAW HER.
- AND WHAT HAPPENED ?

868
01:03:13,390 --> 01:03:15,826
[ Knocking ]

869
01:03:15,860 --> 01:03:17,561
HEY.

870
01:03:17,594 --> 01:03:20,164
HEY.

871
01:03:20,197 --> 01:03:22,532
JUST THOUGHT YOU MIGHT WANT
SOME DRY CLOTHES.

872
01:03:22,566 --> 01:03:24,801
THANKS.
YEAH.

873
01:03:27,905 --> 01:03:29,506
I'M FINE.

874
01:03:29,539 --> 01:03:31,575
I'M OKAY.

875
01:03:35,145 --> 01:03:37,447
I KNOW.

876
01:03:39,349 --> 01:03:41,351
REALLY, I'M OKAY.

877
01:03:46,891 --> 01:03:48,959
[ Sniffles ]

878
01:03:53,330 --> 01:03:56,066
WHAT HAPPENED ?

879
01:04:02,239 --> 01:04:04,108
SHE SAID...

880
01:04:05,509 --> 01:04:07,577
THAT SHE NEVER WANTED ME.

881
01:04:12,249 --> 01:04:17,888
SHE SAID THAT MY FATHER
MADE HER HAVE ME...

882
01:04:19,256 --> 01:04:22,359
AND THAT I WAS
JUST A MISTAKE.

883
01:04:22,392 --> 01:04:24,461
[ Sobbing ]

884
01:04:41,411 --> 01:04:44,481
I LOOK LIKE HER,
YOU KNOW ?

885
01:04:45,515 --> 01:04:49,419
I HAVE HER EYES
AND HER HANDS.

886
01:04:49,453 --> 01:04:51,621
IT'S HER LOSS, LUCE.

887
01:04:51,655 --> 01:04:55,159
IT'S WEIRD THOUGH,
YOU KNOW ?

888
01:04:56,726 --> 01:04:58,662
I DON'T HAVE A MOTHER.

889
01:04:58,695 --> 01:05:02,566
- WELL, YOU HAVE US.
- YEAH.

890
01:05:11,575 --> 01:05:13,243
[ Sighs ]

891
01:05:15,579 --> 01:05:19,449
- HEY.
- HEY.

892
01:05:20,417 --> 01:05:22,652
TRYING TO CALL YOUR DAD ?

893
01:05:22,686 --> 01:05:25,956
I CAN'T.
I WILL IN A MINUTE.

894
01:05:25,990 --> 01:05:28,592
LISTEN, YOU GOT THAT POEM
YOU READ ME ?

895
01:05:28,625 --> 01:05:31,061
YEAH.
CAN I SEE IT ?

896
01:05:31,095 --> 01:05:33,230
YEAH, SURE.

897
01:05:33,263 --> 01:05:36,266
IT'S RIGHT... HERE.

898
01:05:40,104 --> 01:05:41,705
WHAT ARE YOU DOING ?

899
01:05:43,173 --> 01:05:45,475
STOP WORRYING SO MUCH.
COME ON.
I MADE YOU SOMETHING.

900
01:05:45,509 --> 01:05:47,577
OKAY.

901
01:05:52,349 --> 01:05:55,185
THIS IS MY SURPRISE ?

902
01:05:55,219 --> 01:05:57,254
[ Laughs ]
WOULDN'T IT BE SAD
IF IT WAS ?

903
01:05:57,287 --> 01:06:00,190
LIKE IF I JUST TOTALLY SUCKED
AT CHEERING PEOPLE UP.

904
01:06:00,224 --> 01:06:02,592
NO, I, UH--

905
01:06:02,626 --> 01:06:05,629
I WROTE SOME MUSIC
FOR YOUR POEM.

906
01:06:08,232 --> 01:06:10,267
WILL YOU PLAY IT FOR ME ?

907
01:06:10,300 --> 01:06:14,971
WILL YOU SING ?
OKAY.

908
01:06:17,541 --> 01:06:20,544
JUST, UM, USE THIS PART
AS THE CHORUS.

909
01:06:20,577 --> 01:06:23,247
OKAY ?
OKAY.

910
01:06:32,089 --> 01:06:35,559
* NA-NA-NA-NA
LIKE THAT ?
YEAH.

911
01:06:35,592 --> 01:06:38,995
** [ Continues Playing ]

912
01:06:40,497 --> 01:06:44,668
** [ Singing Along ]

913
01:06:47,771 --> 01:06:51,541
** [ Continuing ]

914
01:06:55,679 --> 01:06:59,583
* GO MY WAY
LIKE THAT ?

915
01:07:01,485 --> 01:07:05,655
* IT FEELS LIKE I'M CAUGHT
IN THE MIDDLE *

916
01:07:05,689 --> 01:07:07,691
A LITTLE LOW THERE.
[ Giggles ]

917
01:07:07,724 --> 01:07:12,496
* THAT'S WHEN I REALIZE

918
01:07:12,529 --> 01:07:16,066
* I'M NOT A GIRL

919
01:07:18,602 --> 01:07:21,705
* AND NOT YET A WOMAN

920
01:07:25,409 --> 01:07:28,578
* ALL I NEED IS TIME

921
01:07:28,612 --> 01:07:32,116
* A MOMENT THAT IS MINE

922
01:07:32,149 --> 01:07:36,486
* WHILE I'M IN BETWEEN

923
01:07:36,520 --> 01:07:40,390
* I'M NOT A GIRL *

924
01:07:50,734 --> 01:07:52,769
THANK YOU.

925
01:07:54,671 --> 01:07:57,341
IT'S NO TROUBLE AT ALL.

926
01:08:35,712 --> 01:08:37,781
[ Line Ringing ]

927
01:08:39,449 --> 01:08:43,487
HELLO, YOU HAVE REACHED
PETE AND LUCY.
PLEASE LEAVE A MESSAGE.

928
01:08:43,520 --> 01:08:45,755
[ Machine Beeps ]
HI, POP.

929
01:08:45,789 --> 01:08:50,327
I'M JUST CALLING TO SAY
THAT I'M FINE, OKAY ?

930
01:08:50,360 --> 01:08:55,665
AND YOU WERE RIGHT
ABOUT MAMA.
YOU WERE RIGHT.

931
01:08:55,699 --> 01:09:01,371
I LOVE YOU, OKAY ?
I'M FINE. BYE.

932
01:09:01,405 --> 01:09:03,340
** [ Hard Rock ]

933
01:09:08,278 --> 01:09:11,915
* I'M NOT THE KIND OF GIRL
YOU TAKE HOME *

934
01:09:11,948 --> 01:09:16,886
* IF IT MAKES YOU HAPPY

935
01:09:16,920 --> 01:09:21,258
* IT CAN'T BE THAT BAD

936
01:09:21,291 --> 01:09:26,463
* IF IT MAKES YOU HAPPY

937
01:09:26,496 --> 01:09:30,734
* THEN WHY THE HELL
ARE YOU SO SAD *

938
01:09:31,968 --> 01:09:36,740
* IF IT MAKES YOU HAPPY

939
01:09:36,773 --> 01:09:41,645
* IT CAN'T BE THAT BAD

940
01:09:41,678 --> 01:09:46,550
* IF IT MAKES YOU HAPPY

941
01:09:46,583 --> 01:09:51,755
* THEN WHY THE HELL
ARE YOU SO SAD **

942
01:09:57,794 --> 01:09:59,363
WHOO !

943
01:10:24,588 --> 01:10:26,523
[ Shouting, Laughing ]

944
01:10:31,328 --> 01:10:33,497
IT'S TOO COLD.
IT'S FREEZING !

945
01:10:37,934 --> 01:10:39,969
[ Laughing ]
DON'T EVEN ! DON'T.

946
01:10:42,306 --> 01:10:45,509
I CAN'T BELIEVE
WE'RE FINALLY HERE.
I KNOW.

947
01:10:47,944 --> 01:10:51,014
BEN, YOU KNOW, THERE ARE
A LOT OF COLLEGES HERE IN L.A.

948
01:10:52,316 --> 01:10:53,983
YEAH.

949
01:10:54,017 --> 01:10:56,653
HEY, WHAT IF
I DIDN'T GO BACK ?

950
01:10:56,686 --> 01:10:59,289
I COULD GO TO SCHOOL HERE.

951
01:10:59,323 --> 01:11:01,024
I MEAN,

952
01:11:01,057 --> 01:11:04,928
WHY DON'T I DO SOMETHING
FOR ME FOR ONCE, YOU KNOW ?

953
01:11:04,961 --> 01:11:07,397
I WANNA STAY.

954
01:11:07,431 --> 01:11:09,265
I'M GONNA STAY.

955
01:11:11,868 --> 01:11:13,837
GOOD.

956
01:11:13,870 --> 01:11:18,875
LOOK HOW HAPPY SHE IS.
[ Laughing ]

957
01:11:19,976 --> 01:11:22,446
[ Squealing ]
NO !

958
01:11:22,479 --> 01:11:25,515
FILL THIS OUT,
TURN IT IN OVER THERE.

959
01:11:25,549 --> 01:11:29,786
THE AUDITION IS IN SIX DAYS.
OKAY, WAIT.
WHERE DO WE TURN IT IN ?

960
01:11:29,819 --> 01:11:32,856
YOU TURN IT IN OVER THERE.
[ Sighs ]

961
01:11:32,889 --> 01:11:34,858
FILL THIS OUT--

962
01:11:34,891 --> 01:11:37,927
WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO
ABOUT MUSIC ?
UM, YOU KNOW WHAT ?

963
01:11:37,961 --> 01:11:41,531
I'M GONNA GET
SOME FLYERS PRINTED UP.
I KNOW A FEW GUYS IN L.A.

964
01:11:41,565 --> 01:11:44,368
I'M GONNA TRY TO PUT
A BAND TOGETHER, AND I'LL
SEE YOU BACK AT THE HOTEL.

965
01:11:44,401 --> 01:11:47,971
OKAY. GREAT.
HEY, WHERE YOU GOING ?

966
01:11:58,548 --> 01:12:02,686
BABY ? HI, IT'S ME !
GUESS WHERE I AM.

967
01:12:02,719 --> 01:12:04,588
L.A. !

968
01:12:06,623 --> 01:12:09,058
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.
THEN I'LL COME TO YOU.

969
01:12:11,428 --> 01:12:14,464
ALL RIGHT.
THEN HOW 'BOUT TONIGHT ?

970
01:12:16,566 --> 01:12:19,035
THEN HOW 'BOUT
TOMORROW MORNING ?

971
01:12:21,738 --> 01:12:24,808
DYLAN, I'M IN LOS ANGELES !

972
01:12:24,841 --> 01:12:27,577
I CAME TO SEE YOU !

973
01:12:29,679 --> 01:12:32,649
FINE.

974
01:12:32,682 --> 01:12:34,951
WHAT AM I GONNA SAY ?
FINE.

975
01:12:36,753 --> 01:12:38,655
ME TOO.

976
01:12:46,496 --> 01:12:50,534
HE'S REALLY BUSY
WITH FINALS AND ALL.
YEAH.

977
01:12:50,567 --> 01:12:53,002
WE'RE FINE.

978
01:12:53,036 --> 01:12:57,040
[ Sighs ]
SO WHO WANTS TO GO SIGHTSEEING ?

979
01:12:57,073 --> 01:13:00,076
I DO !
OKAY ! ALL RIGHT.
LUCY ?

980
01:13:01,210 --> 01:13:04,948
- I'M KINDA TIRED.
- OH, BEN ?

981
01:13:04,981 --> 01:13:08,652
YEAH, I'M PRETTY... BEAT.

982
01:13:08,685 --> 01:13:11,387
WELL, I NEED YOU.
WE CAN'T DRIVE YOUR CAR,
REMEMBER ?

983
01:13:13,089 --> 01:13:17,093
- DON'T WRECK IT.
- [ Gasps ]
ALL RIGHT !

984
01:13:19,128 --> 01:13:21,965
[ Horn Honking ]

985
01:13:27,036 --> 01:13:29,072
[ Mimi ]
WAIT, WE'RE ON MELROSE--

986
01:13:29,105 --> 01:13:32,509
I THOUGHT WE WERE GOING
TO SEE THE HOLLYWOOD SIGN.

987
01:13:32,542 --> 01:13:36,446
WE WILL.
BUT I THINK IT'S
BACK THAT WAY.

988
01:13:36,480 --> 01:13:39,716
I KNOW.
BUT WE'RE GONNA MAKE
A STOP FIRST, OKAY ?

989
01:13:40,950 --> 01:13:43,520
KIT, YOU CAN
SEE DYLAN TOMORROW.

990
01:13:43,553 --> 01:13:45,455
[ Sighs ]

991
01:13:45,489 --> 01:13:47,123
- KIT, COME ON.
LET'S GO BACK.
- NO.

992
01:13:47,156 --> 01:13:51,995
- KIT, PLEASE, LET'S GO BACK.
PLEASE !
- NO ! I WANT TO SEE HIM NOW.

993
01:14:06,843 --> 01:14:08,712
ARE YOU SURE ?

994
01:14:09,779 --> 01:14:11,615
YEAH.

995
01:14:11,648 --> 01:14:15,819
* I AM A WOMAN WITH A MISSION

996
01:14:15,852 --> 01:14:18,087
* AND A PAST TO OUTDO

997
01:14:18,121 --> 01:14:24,227
* I DON'T NEED A GUN
I GOT A MICROPHONE
AND A MELODY OR TWO *

998
01:14:24,260 --> 01:14:28,131
* JUST LIKE THE EARTH HAS SPENT
A THOUSAND YEARS *

999
01:14:28,164 --> 01:14:31,134
* MAKING UP FOR WHAT WE DO

1000
01:14:34,738 --> 01:14:37,741
* SO HAVE I FOR YOU

1001
01:14:40,009 --> 01:14:42,045
* OH-OH-OH
* SO HAVE I

1002
01:14:42,078 --> 01:14:46,149
* MAMA
YOU CAN CHOOSE THE RAIN *

1003
01:14:46,182 --> 01:14:50,820
* BUT I CHOOSE THE SUN *

1004
01:14:53,857 --> 01:14:57,694
- KIT, I REALLY SHOULD
WAIT IN THE CAR. COME ON.
- NO, MIMI.

1005
01:14:57,727 --> 01:15:00,764
HOW DO I LOOK ?
YOU LOOK REALLY GREAT,
BUT KIT,

1006
01:15:00,797 --> 01:15:04,968
DON'T YOU THINK YOU GUYS MIGHT
WANT TO BE ALONE TOGETHER ?
NO.

1007
01:15:05,001 --> 01:15:08,772
I WANT YOU WITH ME.
COME ON.

1008
01:15:19,015 --> 01:15:21,284
- SURPRISE !
- HONEY.

1009
01:15:21,317 --> 01:15:24,187
UM--
HI ! OH, BABY.

1010
01:15:24,220 --> 01:15:26,690
KIT-KAT, I THOUGHT WE WERE
GONNA MAKE PLANS TOMORROW.

1011
01:15:26,723 --> 01:15:30,760
OH, I KNOW.
I JUST REALLY WANTED TO SEE YOU.
THIS IS MY FRIEND, MIMI.

1012
01:15:30,794 --> 01:15:33,096
- MIMI. HEY.
- HEY.

1013
01:15:33,129 --> 01:15:38,101
- YOU TWO KNOW EACH OTHER ?
- YEAH. F-FROM-FROM SCHOOL.
RIGHT, MIMI ?

1014
01:15:38,134 --> 01:15:41,537
- RIGHT.
- YEAH.

1015
01:15:43,707 --> 01:15:47,043
OH. WELL, AREN'T YOU
GONNA INVITE US IN ?

1016
01:15:47,076 --> 01:15:50,847
YEAH, I WOULD, KITTY-KAT,
BUT I'VE GOT THIS FRIEND HERE,
AND HE'S--

1017
01:15:50,880 --> 01:15:53,049
YOU KNOW, HE'S REALLY UPSET,
AND WE'RE SUPPOSED TO, LIKE,

1018
01:15:53,082 --> 01:15:54,918
YOU KNOW,
HANG OUT OR WHATEVER.

1019
01:15:54,951 --> 01:15:58,688
- OH.
- [ Woman ] DO YOU NEED MONEY
FOR THE PIZZA ?

1020
01:16:00,123 --> 01:16:03,126
YOUR FRIEND SOUNDS
REALLY UPSET.

1021
01:16:03,159 --> 01:16:05,662
WAIT, KIT, HOLD ON.
[ Groans ]

1022
01:16:05,695 --> 01:16:09,332
- OH, GOD.
- WHO'S SHE ?

1023
01:16:11,234 --> 01:16:13,803
WE'RE SUPPOSED TO BE
GETTING MARRIED.

1024
01:16:15,639 --> 01:16:18,041
WE'RE SUPPOSED TO BE
GETTING MARRIED.

1025
01:16:18,074 --> 01:16:22,879
I WAS-- I WAS GONNA TELL YOU,
I JUST, YOU KNOW, DIDN'T
WANT TO DO IT OVER THE PHONE.

1026
01:16:22,912 --> 01:16:27,617
DYLAN, YOU GAVE ME A RING.
YOU PROPOSED,
AND YOU GAVE ME A RING !

1027
01:16:27,651 --> 01:16:31,287
KIT, I MEAN,
I'M SORRY, YOU KNOW ?

1028
01:16:37,126 --> 01:16:39,663
OH, MY GOD.

1029
01:16:42,398 --> 01:16:45,735
OH, MY GOD.
OH, MY GOD !

1030
01:16:45,769 --> 01:16:48,972
[ Sobbing ]
IT WAS DYLAN, WASN'T IT ?

1031
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:53,076
- I--
- IT WAS YOU.
YOU WERE THE GUY AT
CHRISTMAS.

1032
01:16:53,109 --> 01:16:57,080
- WASN'T IT ?
IT WAS HIM, HUH ?
- WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT ?

1033
01:16:57,113 --> 01:17:01,250
THAT NIGHT WHEN YOU CAME OVER,
YOU HAD THAT RIP IN YOUR SHIRT.

1034
01:17:01,284 --> 01:17:05,188
THAT WAS THE NIGHT THAT HE--
KIT, WH-WH-WHAT IS
YOUR PROBLEM HERE ?

1035
01:17:05,221 --> 01:17:10,126
- KIT, I HAVE TO GO.
- NO, MIMI, COME BACK HERE.
MIMI, COME BACK !

1036
01:17:10,159 --> 01:17:13,930
I WANT HIM TO ADMIT IT.
ADMIT IT !

1037
01:17:13,963 --> 01:17:17,333
YOU'RE GETTING YOURSELF
ALL WORKED UP OVER NOTHING,
KITTY-KAT.

1038
01:17:18,868 --> 01:17:22,105
MY NAME IS NOT KITTY-KAT.
I AM NOT YOUR PET !

1039
01:17:22,138 --> 01:17:25,408
[ Sobbing ]
MIMI ! MIMI.

1040
01:17:26,810 --> 01:17:28,778
[ Gasps, Cries Out ]

1041
01:17:30,313 --> 01:17:33,349
[ Siren Wailing ]

1042
01:17:35,351 --> 01:17:37,420
[ Phone Ringing ]

1043
01:17:52,101 --> 01:17:54,003
HELLO ?

1044
01:17:59,809 --> 01:18:01,677
[ Inaudible ]

1045
01:18:09,853 --> 01:18:12,822
EXCUSE ME,
WHERE'S THE PHONE ?
IT'S RIGHT OVER THERE.

1046
01:18:20,496 --> 01:18:23,232
YEAH, CAN I MAKE
A COLLECT CALL, PLEASE ?

1047
01:18:32,275 --> 01:18:34,043
HEY.

1048
01:18:34,077 --> 01:18:35,845
HI.

1049
01:18:42,285 --> 01:18:45,088
THEY SAID I LOST THE BABY.

1050
01:18:45,121 --> 01:18:47,791
[ Scoffs ]
"LOST IT."

1051
01:18:48,858 --> 01:18:52,295
LIKE IT WAS MY KEYS
OR SOMETHING.

1052
01:18:54,363 --> 01:18:58,034
ISN'T THAT THE STUPIDEST
DAMN THING YOU'VE EVER HEARD ?

1053
01:18:59,135 --> 01:19:00,804
YEAH.

1054
01:19:02,305 --> 01:19:04,440
I'D DECIDED TO KEEP HER.

1055
01:19:06,409 --> 01:19:10,046
I WAS STANDING ON THE BEACH,

1056
01:19:10,079 --> 01:19:15,284
AND MY TOES WERE IN THE--
IN THE PACIFIC OCEAN,

1057
01:19:17,420 --> 01:19:19,455
AND SHE KICKED.

1058
01:19:22,158 --> 01:19:24,127
IT WAS LIKE THIS SIGN.

1059
01:19:25,561 --> 01:19:27,897
DON'T TOUCH ME, LUCE.
I'M ALREADY CRYING.

1060
01:19:27,931 --> 01:19:29,966
OKAY.

1061
01:19:29,999 --> 01:19:34,437
[ Sniffles ]
I WOULD HAVE MADE A GOOD MOM.

1062
01:19:35,604 --> 01:19:37,773
YEAH.

1063
01:19:41,144 --> 01:19:43,012
[ Sobs ]

1064
01:19:43,046 --> 01:19:45,448
[ Pete ]
JUST WHAT WERE YOU THINKING,
RUNNING AWAY,

1065
01:19:45,481 --> 01:19:48,451
WITH A PREGNANT GIRL !

1066
01:19:48,484 --> 01:19:50,419
LUCY, I'M WAITING
FOR AN ANSWER.

1067
01:19:50,453 --> 01:19:53,056
DO YOU KNOW WHAT IT TOOK
TO COME HERE ?

1068
01:19:53,089 --> 01:19:56,292
I HAD TO TAKE
CASH OUT OF THE SAVINGS
FOR PLANE FARE AND HOTEL.

1069
01:19:56,325 --> 01:20:00,396
YOU KNOW HOW HARD I WORKED
TO EARN THAT MONEY
FOR YOUR COLLEGE EDUCATION.

1070
01:20:00,429 --> 01:20:03,399
- I'M SORRY.
- [ Sighs ]

1071
01:20:07,003 --> 01:20:10,874
SO YOU MADE A MISTAKE.
I UNDERSTAND.

1072
01:20:11,607 --> 01:20:14,610
EVERYBODY MAKES MISTAKES.

1073
01:20:14,643 --> 01:20:19,315
YOU'RE FORGIVEN.
I'M JUST GONNA TAKE YOU GIRLS
BACK TO WHERE YOU BELONG,

1074
01:20:19,348 --> 01:20:22,318
AND WE'LL FORGET ABOUT
THIS WHOLE CRAZY THING,
ALL RIGHT ?

1075
01:20:22,351 --> 01:20:24,320
OKAY.

1076
01:20:24,353 --> 01:20:25,788
WHO'S THAT BOY
YOU WERE WITH ?

1077
01:20:25,821 --> 01:20:29,993
HOW OLD IS HE ANYWAY ?
IS HE THE ONE WHO PUT
THE CRAZY IDEA IN YOUR HEAD ?

1078
01:20:30,026 --> 01:20:33,196
NO. HE'S--

1079
01:20:33,229 --> 01:20:35,531
